WEBVTT

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:43.350
You never give me nothing but a love and I'm bad to love you.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.350
- You boomer, let's go. - Come on, let's go, you're holding up the game, man.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.650
- Sit down and play. - All right then, let's do it.

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:54.040
- Over here. - You can't play anymore.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.460
- Sit down, I'm sick. - What's the matter with you?

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.400
You can't quit now. - You gotta quit.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:04.580
Cold, cold, I'm sick.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:08.710
He wasn't too sick to walk off the boat and win a hundred and ninety bucks the first night you were in the country.

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:09.810
Was he, Blackie?

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.300
If you bring him fully, you better tell him.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.020
What's the matter with you?

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.060
If you didn't have some meat on it, there'll be trouble, huh?

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:15.480
Sick.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.140
Got a headache back.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:17.960
No.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.800
Look buddy, Blackie don't like it.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:26.450
Blackie don't like nobody to walk out of a game just like that.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.870
I'll talk to him, Blackie, I'll get him back.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:54.230
Oh, no.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:14.500
- I want that money. - All right, let's get it.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.000
- Hey, that was...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.290
- Strong? - Nah, shot twice. Must've crawled on this thing.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.290
- Recognize him? - Nah, he ain't from around here.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:38.790
He's some kind of foreigner.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:41.280
- Foreigner, huh? - Yeah, something like that.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:45.100
- Call the meat bag, will ya? - Come on, folks. Let's get moving over there. Break it up.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:50.100
- Let's go, let's go now. - Hey, Matt standing in that water ain't good for a cold.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.100
- What is it? - Come on, Joe. Get him out of there.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:00.000
Eddie?

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:04.290
- Let's go, man. - Trouble with that little boy is he just don't realize the honeymoon is over.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:08.260
I said to him, "Man, if you want to sell me a car, you're going to have to really sell it to me."

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.560
- 'Cause I'm just sitting back and watching. Yes, sir. - That's telling him, boy.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:13.890
You're working too hard again, Jerry. Thank you.

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:17.690
- Will you be able to make it for lunch? - Well, I gotta dig a couple of bullets out of this guy's chest.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:20.290
May take 30, 40 minutes. Yeah, I guess I can make it.

00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:22.390
Don't waste any time 'cause I'm real hungry.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:41.840
- Where do you want to go? - Why do you want to eat?

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:45.640
That place down the street's okay. I kinda like that spaghetti.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.080
Yeah, that's him.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.650
I figured we might try to rendezvous again.

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:52.070
You interested in food or talking to that waitress?

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:54.030
Oh, no, you don't think I know of me, Cleaver.

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.020
You're the guy she really went for.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:00.000
Maybe, but I don't know how she ever saw me the way you kept sticking your head.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.620
- Put my elbow on my face. - Okay, okay, you win.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:05.660
We'll try the spaghetti, okay?

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.350
Hey, Cleaver, okay?

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:14.560
Maybe not. This may take a little longer than I thought.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.190
All right, I'll wait for you.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:19.650
- That the foreigner that just brought in, Cleaver? - Yeah, better stay away from him.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.150
- Got a cat. - I said stay away from him.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.220
- What's the matter? I've got a cat. - Look, stay away from him. Get out.

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.470
- What's wrong with you? - Just stay out.

00:07:45.160 --> 00:07:50.710
There's no brush wrong, Pop.

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:56.500
You got too much paint on it.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.370
- How's that?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:58.210
- Better.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.130
- Thank you.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.000
- Mr. Redfield says

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:04.450
- It's the worst thing you can do to get too much paint on the brush. - Is that right?

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:09.150
- Mm-hmm. Why don't you let me do it for you?

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:14.920
- Okay. You better take it easy now. You don't want to get paint all over those pants.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:17.970
- Hiya, Tommy. - Hi, Mr. Redfield.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.970
- Eating your pop-hot paint? - Sure.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.010
- Hello, Doctor. - How are you?

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:23.930
- Great boy you have there. - Thank you, thank you.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:28.710
- See you Saturday, Mr. Redfield. - Sure, sure. Anytime you like.

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:30.000
If things get dull, just drop off.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.880
Pop, right on over here.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:36.110
- Who's that? - Mr. Redfield.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.850
- He's a painter. - Yeah, so I gather.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:41.770
He lives in the big house down on the corner.

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:43.300
You ought to see it, Pop.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:45.300
It's full of all kinds of stuff.

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:49.080
And he has electric trains and everything.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.410
Must be great.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:52.250
Hey, you know what I think's the matter with this stuff?

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:53.370
- What? - It's too thick.

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:54.910
- Nah. - It's too thick.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:57.060
Look at it, I'm gonna thin it.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:59.440
On the turpin time, huh.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:11.200
electric train shit not here it's got me from the office tell him i went to alaska

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:23.500
it's waiting plan problem can i have a quarter what happened to your allowance it's for the

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:30.000
movies pop all the kids are going oh come on now look old boy you're supposed to get

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.800
You get 50 cents a week.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:35.000
Oh, Pop, money just goes. You know how it is.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.270
Yeah, I got a pretty good idea.

00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:43.380
Come on. You're a pest.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.350
Thanks, Pop. I knew you would.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:48.400
Yeah, I knew it, too.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.400
First day I've had off in six weeks.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.290
I'm just about getting used to it when the phone rings.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.290
What am I supposed to be, anyhow?

00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:57.300
The only one in that office that knows what to do?

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.300
Tell Gaffney. He called, not me.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.000
I should have had a disconnect.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.320
Paul, I thought I was going to take the whole day off.

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:09.410
Oh, yeah.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:13.880
What do you mean, there's something funny about it?

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:22.400
Yeah, well, all right, I'll come down.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:26.630
Hold everybody there that had any contact with the body in case it is something.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:28.800
No, I'd rather you stay there.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.710
Yeah, I know. It's all right.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.860
- I'll see you. - Are you serious?

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:40.670
No, it's always a crisis with those boys when they can't diagnose something.

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:43.960
Don't suppose that cleaner remembered to bring back my...

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.850
- Well, what happened to him all of a sudden? - Go ahead and change. I'll bring it in.

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:50.570
Hey, Mom, this lunch ready yet?

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:52.720
Oh, you and your father.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:57.560
There's no hunting today where they're down in the bayous.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:59.960
I know, I know. What's the rush?

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.450
- What are you planning to use for money? - Oh, I got it!

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:10.280
No, I told him I'm just going to stay home and lie around all day.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:16.310
I'm not going to shave, I'm going to get out of my clothes and drink a couple of drinks.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:21.000
Now, what? Take a little nap in the afternoon, have an early dinner.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:25.500
Just take the whole day off. Relax, you know what I mean?

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:29.920
- Did you give Tommy a quarter for the movies? - Well, I...

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:32.790
- Yeah. - Weren't you the one that decided

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:35.820
we'd give him a regular allowance to teach him about money?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:37.990
- Well, yeah, I did. - Look, Hank.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:41.170
He may be an only child, but I'm not going to have him act like one here.

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:43.470
I gave you the answer to that one two years ago.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:45.390
- Yeah. - Yeah.

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:47.790
I'm getting tired of always being the heavy in the piece.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.730
Okay, okay.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:52.630
Incidentally, since you're being so free with your money...

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:58.070
What? I only smoked a pill from Whitfield's.

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:00.000
- Uh-huh, the same one. - Well, that'll be right.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.340
- What's your allowance? - You're kidding, of course.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.950
$42, and I'm fresh out.

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:06.710
- Again? - Still.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.710
And you've been promising to pay, Clint.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:11.630
It's getting embarrassing, really. I'm afraid to go down to the store.

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:14.970
What, for $42? Let 'em wait.

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:19.690
I never saw the day old Massa Whitfield broke his neck getting anything over here.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:24.000
$42. Listen, one of these days we'll walk into that store and pay...

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:28.370
- One of what days? - Oh, one of these days.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.000
Uh-huh. When one of those days...

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:33.780
The oil companies decide that they can't lay a pipeline in Arabia...

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.780
...without the services of Dr. Clinton Reed.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:42.770
A man with a high forehead and the disposition of an old honey.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:47.700
Hey, Clint. I like high foreheads.

00:12:47.900 --> 00:12:49.190
Yeah, I bet you do.

00:12:49.450 --> 00:12:51.190
Well, it happens. Don't think it doesn't.

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:53.390
They've taken a lot of guys from the department.

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:56.310
Bill Moseley works for an industrial chemical company.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:13:00.000
- I know they have. - Well, it happened to me, too.

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:05.810
- Just like having another baby. - One of these days, huh?

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:12.240
- You're a fresh dame. - Pretty, though, hmm?

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:17.960
You're just about to get by. I gotta get out of here.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:19.810
- Hey. - What?

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:25.220
- Try and get in early if you can, Mosh. - Yeah, I'll try.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:36.260
- Why don't you let Tommy have this quarter?

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:39.280
- Why don't you get out of here?

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:40.470
- Bye. - Bye.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.060
Yeah. Well, that's life, that's pork.

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:04.810
Well, I gotta get through it.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:05.810
Call me, dear.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:09.780
Don't sit through it more than twice.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:10.890
Will you, dear?

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:17.860
What do you make of that tissue, Ben?

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:19.860
I don't know, but I don't like it.

00:14:19.860 --> 00:14:21.750
This one's a specimen of his sputum.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.750
And here's one of the bullets Cleaver recovered.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.750
Oh, yeah, let me see that slide.

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:46.410
- Get 'em away from that body. - Okay, fellas, that's all. Let's go.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:52.820
- Just wait outside for a minute, will you, fellas, with the others? - Any way to pull these shapes?

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:57.670
- Sure, Di. - Can you get this man's remated?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.000
- Well, I suppose. - I don't want anything.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:04.050
I want his teammates right now. Set it up, will you?

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:05.220
Oh, Cleaver.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:06.160
Yes?

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:08.160
I want everything that's touched him burned or sterilized, do you understand?

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:09.060
Sure.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:17.350
Paul, get those slides into a sterilizer right away, will you?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.690
Right.

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:21.690
Oh, say, they sent over the serum and streptomyosin.

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:22.840
Good.

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:23.840
Hey, Cleaver, what's going on around here?

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:25.840
A report on who killed this man, Sergeant?

00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:26.790
No.

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:27.690
Any leaves?

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:29.500
No, sir. I don't think so.

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:30.000
Well, do you know?

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:34.910
don't you this is important well sure has anyone been able to identify the body no sir nobody

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:42.560
sent the fingerprints off to the fbi but haven't heard anything from yet you got everybody here

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:47.230
who had anything to do with the body yeah fingerprint men photographers patrolman who

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:54.260
found him nearly everybody what do you mean nearly it was billy hall he had him now yes now right away

00:15:55.830 --> 00:16:00.000
call billy hall i haven't come down right away now yeah right now thanks we had these people

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:02.350
- Go line up, please. - All right, let's follow the line, fellas.

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:04.510
Come on, shake it up here. Press the line here.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:07.500
Hey, this is Dr. Reeve, the government health service.

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:08.580
This will only take a minute.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:11.000
As a precautionary, Benger, we're going to inoculate all of you.

00:16:11.080 --> 00:16:13.730
So if you just take your coats off, roll off your sleeves.

00:16:13.810 --> 00:16:15.850
Hurry up, Paul. Let's start asking questions.

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:17.690
Oh, Cleaver, would you mind helping out?

00:16:17.770 --> 00:16:19.430
- Okay, ma'am. - And, uh, thanks.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:21.670
That was a fine job. You did just the right thing.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:23.930
- Oh, thank you. - I appreciate it.

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:27.430
Give me two CCs. I fixed it to have him cremated.

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:29.860
Swell. Help Cleaver now at the end, will you, Ben?

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:34.080
- Here's the alcohol. - All right, let's get this over with quickly, please.

00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:37.700
- Give me the first one, Paul. - What's in them things, Doctor?

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:40.380
- I think just a little serum. - Serum for what?

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:43.660
- I told you, precautionary measure. - Yeah, precautionary, but for what?

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:46.800
- Well, it's possible a dead man may have had some communicable disease.

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:51.640
- I don't have to take none of the shots. - I can quarantine you for ten days.

00:16:51.640 --> 00:17:00.000
Hold still, or this is going to hurt. - Aside from isolated cases...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.590
In the past 20 years, there's been at least one major outbreak.

00:17:03.590 --> 00:17:07.200
In November of 1924 in Los Angeles, California,

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:09.960
a woman died of what was thought to be pneumonia.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:12.550
Thirty-two people had had contact with her.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:16.750
And within four days before the disease could be correctly diagnosed and contained,

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:18.500
26 of them had died.

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:20.900
And they died suddenly, violently, and horribly.

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:24.230
The disease was finally found to be pneumonic plague.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:27.360
Pneumonic plague is the pulmonary form of bubonic,

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:30.000
the black death of the Middle Ages, and its death incident

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:34.930
- Who didn't you say he was? - I'm Dr. Reed of the United States Public Health Service.

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:37.930
And one of the jobs of my department is to keep plague out of this country.

00:17:37.950 --> 00:17:39.930
Sit down, sit down. Don't let me interrupt you.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.880
Speak your water later, will you, please?

00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:43.770
Come on, Mary.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.770
Has Dr. Reed filled you in on this?

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:46.600
Are you finished, Doctor?

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:48.600
Well, there's not much more, Mr. Mayor.

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:51.680
Bubonic plague, as you probably know, is spread by the rat flea,

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:54.680
which is why we watch all ships and ports.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:18:00.000
Pneumonic, on the contrary, can be spread like a common cold on the breath,

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.000
sneezes, or sputum of its victims.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:05.000
Very interesting, but I don't quite see why we were calling to this.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:06.980
Because this morning, right here in the city,

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:09.920
your police found the body of a man who was infected with this disease.

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:12.000
Well, Dan, what about him?

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.000
Our reports show the man died with two bullet wounds.

00:18:14.000 --> 00:18:16.000
He did, heart and lungs.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:18.000
Death was probably instantaneous, right, Tom?

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:20.000
Yes, sir. We had a police surgeon there.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:23.000
Regardless of what the police surgeon said, he would have died within 12 hours.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.000
But what he did die of was two bullet holes.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.000
- He had pneumonic plague. - But he died of...

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.570
- I'll bet, Tom. - Dr. Mackey?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.000
No, Mr. Mayor, I wasn't there.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:34.700
Ben was there when the body was brought in, but I can go now and check.

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:35.900
I had the body destroyed.

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:37.300
- You had it destroyed. - Destroyed?

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:39.200
It was a prime source of contamination.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:41.180
- I had Ben cremated. - I see.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.580
What else have you done, Mackey?

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:44.680
- Why, I believe... - Everyone who came in contact with the body

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.180
has been inoculated. - That's right.

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.780
Everyone we knew of with serum and streptomyosin.

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:49.480
And now I think they ought to be isolated.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.280
We can have them watched. We know who they are.

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:52.760
All but one.

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:55.450
The man who killed him, or men.

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:56.850
Mr. Mayor, this man was shot.

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:59.460
The killer wasn't within 10 feet of him. I can prove it.

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:00.000
Was he shot?

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:05.040
that river bag captain of course not he was dumped off the canal street pier about 5 5 30.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:12.620
how did he get to the canal street pier how do i know somebody must have the point is that whoever

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:17.180
dumped him there may very well be walking around with incipient plague at this moment on our way

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:24.170
the moment no we've got to work on the supposition the doctor's right then looks like your job

00:19:24.170 --> 00:19:30.000
all right sir i'll do what i can but after all we don't know the identity of the dead

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.990
We have no possible idea of the motivation.

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:34.990
And you haven't got much time, Mr. Quinn.

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:37.990
Also, we haven't got the body.

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:40.070
Did you empty out his pockets?

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:42.070
- I had everything burned. - Great.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:44.070
If the killer is incubating pneumonic plague,

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:46.070
he can start spreading it within 48 hours.

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:49.070
- 48 hours? - Yes, we have 48 hours.

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:50.920
Shortly after that, you'll have the makings of an epidemic.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:53.860
Commissioner, what's the use of kidding ourselves?

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:55.860
We can't turn up an unknown killer in two days.

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:57.870
He's absolutely right, Mr. Mayor.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:00.000
The police department can't do it.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.580
can't be held responsible for this.

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:03.720
Now, if you want to believe the doctor here,

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:07.350
I'm sorry, sir, but frankly, I honestly don't.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:08.860
But if you want to believe him,

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.740
there's only one way to handle this.

00:20:11.250 --> 00:20:12.670
Give the story to the press.

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:13.910
You get on the radio.

00:20:14.030 --> 00:20:15.510
And have everybody who was in contact

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:16.850
with a dead man leave town?

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:18.530
You can't give it to the press.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.230
Now, I may be an alarmist.

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:22.150
I may be entirely wrong about the whole matter,

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:23.770
but I've seen this disease work.

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:25.710
And I'm telling you, if it ever gets loose,

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:27.550
it can spread over the entire country.

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:29.410
And the result will be more horrible

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:30.000
than any of you can do.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:38.550
imagine. And the key to the whole thing lies right here, now, in the next 48 hours. You

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:49.780
can take me at my word, whatever you like. What can we do? Find this man. Dan, put your

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:55.240
best man on him. Yes, sir. Tom, you work with the doctor. Anything else you need, ask for

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:59.310
it. Mackie. Thank you. We'll give him all the assistance possible. That's it, gentlemen.

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:00.000
All right.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:01.950
Tom, make your arrangements with the doctor here.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.970
I'll be on call waiting for a report.

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:06.360
Take any emergency action you feel necessary.

00:21:06.400 --> 00:21:23.040
- Annapolis, ma'am? - No.

00:21:23.270 --> 00:21:27.430
- Why? - No reason.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:34.360
- Hope I wasn't too rough. - On me?

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:38.320
- No. - No, I meant the rest of 'em.

00:21:39.300 --> 00:21:41.990
I still have a feeling they don't believe me.

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:45.840
I just know how serious this can be. I was trying to put it across to 'em.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:52.810
Mm-hmm.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:56.760
Now I'd start worrying about what you're gonna do when we don't turn up with your boy.

00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:06.390
- No, Josh. - This is the attitude you're gonna start.

00:22:06.490 --> 00:22:08.790
- Now, Whit, we're not gonna get there. - Just to read, I was assigned to this.

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:13.090
I'll do the best I can, but let's not get the idea that I'm a sailor in your, uh, Navy.

00:22:13.190 --> 00:22:14.890
- Now, wait a minute. - Hello, Warren. I've been looking for you.

00:22:14.990 --> 00:22:17.390
- You found me and you're interrupting me. - Heard you had a meeting.

00:22:17.490 --> 00:22:20.120
- Little pictures. - Had Mackey and the Board of Health in, too.

00:22:20.220 --> 00:22:22.220
- What's the score? - Some complaints about your newspaper.

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:23.820
We figured we ought to fumigate it.

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:26.230
Now, now, you know you can't hide anything.

00:22:26.330 --> 00:22:28.230
When it breaks, I'll spell your name wrong.

00:22:28.330 --> 00:22:30.000
That's what I told him. You just ought to fumigate it.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.690
You boys worry me when you take off on your own.

00:22:32.770 --> 00:22:35.270
No sense in our both worrying. Goodbye, Nath.

00:22:35.350 --> 00:22:37.640
- Now, wait a second, Warren. - Goodbye, Nath.

00:22:37.720 --> 00:22:45.640
- Where are you going, Mr. Reed? - I don't know. That depends on you.

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:48.600
Listen, Doctor, I got a job to do, just a routine sort of thing,

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:51.060
like rounding up every possible suspect.

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:53.170
I'm supposed to be pretty good at my job,

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:55.210
so why don't I call you if I need you?

00:22:55.290 --> 00:22:58.120
Are you implying you'd like to get rid of me, Captain?

00:22:58.200 --> 00:23:00.000
No, but...

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:05.570
- That'll go with you. - Come on.

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:11.180
- What do you call that? - Hi, Johnny.

00:23:11.260 --> 00:23:14.140
- Hello, Mr. Smith. How you been seeing? - You call that a concealed weapon?

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:15.730
You think you can hold me on this?

00:23:15.800 --> 00:23:19.880
- Why were you with it last night? - Last night while I was home, shucking oysters.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:22.140
- What goes on here, Charlie? - Who knows?

00:23:22.210 --> 00:23:25.410
- The wife said she didn't come home all night. - She didn't come home all night.

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:26.900
She don't know what she's talking about.

00:23:26.980 --> 00:23:30.000
I tell you, I got a right to a lawyer. You can't just hold me in without a lawyer.

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:33.150
- Oh, why don't you shut up? - You meet a lot of guys.

00:23:33.150 --> 00:23:34.270
You ever see this one?

00:23:34.270 --> 00:23:35.710
What kind of a crack is that?

00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:37.870
So I hang around the roost once in a while?

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:40.030
Does that make me an information bureau?

00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:43.730
Listen, buddy, I have to be a personal friend of Charlie Sweeney's, see?

00:23:43.730 --> 00:23:45.010
And he ain't gonna like me.

00:23:45.410 --> 00:23:48.850
Well, maybe Charlie Sweeney can tell me where you was at last night.

00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:51.070
Why don't you call him and find out?

00:23:51.070 --> 00:23:53.210
He'll have me outta here in 20 minutes.

00:23:53.210 --> 00:23:56.450
Well, for 20 minutes, you'll tell me where you was at last night.

00:23:56.450 --> 00:23:59.410
You can't do this to me. I'm a citizen and I got rights.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:05.440
Raymond Fitch, laundry attendant, 1943, petty larceny, 30 days.

00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:09.090
1945, petty larceny, 90 days.

00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:12.090
- Shall I go any further? - Nah, forget it.

00:24:12.590 --> 00:24:15.520
Mind if I smoke? Trying to get away from cigarettes.

00:24:15.660 --> 00:24:18.550
Put it on. You ever see this guy?

00:24:18.650 --> 00:24:21.040
- No, I never seen this guy. - Well, look.

00:24:21.330 --> 00:24:24.280
I mean, I never seen this guy. What...

00:24:24.380 --> 00:24:25.890
What are you asking me for?

00:24:26.310 --> 00:24:28.520
Kissing like that, you see it, you remember it, huh?

00:24:30.120 --> 00:24:33.920
- How were you last night all night? - Last night? Last night.

00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:37.120
Oh, yeah. I went to see my mother-in-law. She was wrestling semifinals.

00:24:37.200 --> 00:24:39.080
- Where were you? - I was only kidding.

00:24:39.160 --> 00:24:42.720
- Actually, me and my wife went to see... - Where were you, fat boy?

00:24:43.000 --> 00:24:46.720
- What's the matter? You don't believe me? - I think you're a constitutional liar.

00:24:46.800 --> 00:24:49.720
Other people have told me the same thing. I don't mind.

00:24:49.800 --> 00:24:52.150
Of course, the body was burned, so we don't have too much.

00:24:52.230 --> 00:24:56.260
The boys that did examine him say he may be an Armenian, Czech or mixed blood.

00:24:56.340 --> 00:25:00.000
Approximate age 42, height 5'9", weight 143.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:03.510
Suits made in Haifa, shoes in Buenos Aires.

00:25:03.510 --> 00:25:06.080
You ought to notify the immigration authorities immediately.

00:25:06.080 --> 00:25:08.100
- Get with him. - All right.

00:25:08.100 --> 00:25:09.670
Keep going, Scott.

00:25:09.670 --> 00:25:12.470
Mobile, Tampa, and other Gulf ports have no record of him, sir.

00:25:12.470 --> 00:25:13.970
- Anything else? - Well, let's see.

00:25:13.970 --> 00:25:15.670
The FBI has no record of him.

00:25:15.670 --> 00:25:20.270
Our lab found traces of fish, rust-resistant paint, and salt in his clothes.

00:25:20.270 --> 00:25:21.670
The fish traces could be shrimp.

00:25:21.670 --> 00:25:23.970
Well, it's certainly positive he came in off a boat, so we wouldn't...

00:25:23.970 --> 00:25:26.970
Unless he walked through a fish market, bought four pounds of shrimp,

00:25:26.970 --> 00:25:29.640
and brushed against a freshly painted fire escape.

00:25:30.060 --> 00:25:33.020
- I suppose those are all the photographs we have. - Those are the only ones, sir.

00:25:33.100 --> 00:25:35.320
- The emergency ships are coming in now, sir. - Okay.

00:25:35.400 --> 00:25:41.940
Oh, um, Captain, the, um, the boys are sort of wondering why they have to take these shots.

00:25:42.020 --> 00:25:44.060
They've been wondering, have they? Where do they think they are?

00:25:44.140 --> 00:25:46.980
In a summer camp? Because the Commissioner said so, that's why.

00:25:47.060 --> 00:25:48.280
- That's what I told them. - Yes, sir.

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:51.600
What's the matter? They're afraid of a little needle? They've been wondering.

00:25:53.400 --> 00:25:55.720
- Roll up your sleeve. - What do you mean? What do you think you're gonna do?

00:25:55.800 --> 00:25:58.410
- Roll up your sleeve. - Why should I take one of those things?

00:25:58.490 --> 00:26:00.000
Because the Commissioner said so.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:01.970
and I told the commissioner.

00:26:02.870 --> 00:26:03.570
Roll it up.

00:26:07.830 --> 00:26:08.890
Anything funny, Scott?

00:26:09.340 --> 00:26:09.680
No, sir.

00:26:09.860 --> 00:26:10.160
No, sir.

00:26:16.580 --> 00:26:18.260
Oh, brother, this I've got to see.

00:26:20.330 --> 00:26:22.020
What's the matter?

00:26:22.060 --> 00:26:23.380
You guys ain't got enough work to do?

00:26:23.480 --> 00:26:23.900
Yes, sir.

00:26:24.020 --> 00:26:24.560
Funny how we got it.

00:26:24.580 --> 00:26:25.300
Well, get on it.

00:26:26.940 --> 00:26:28.770
Yeah, how about that?

00:26:28.910 --> 00:26:30.000
Well, you can't say you're not getting

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:32.700
There's half the two-bit criminals in town.

00:26:32.800 --> 00:26:34.700
More of them coming through.

00:26:34.800 --> 00:26:37.180
I wish you sounded more confident of getting information.

00:26:37.280 --> 00:26:38.680
Information? We'll get plenty of it.

00:26:38.780 --> 00:26:41.480
About pickpockets, sneak thieves, wife beaters.

00:26:41.580 --> 00:26:44.900
But about your murderer? Not a chance.

00:26:45.000 --> 00:26:55.180
That isn't gonna work. What are you doing?

00:26:55.280 --> 00:26:57.380
I'm doing it because the commissioner told me to.

00:26:57.490 --> 00:27:00.000
And I'm doing it this way because it's the only way you left me.

00:27:00.320 --> 00:27:01.740
Why I'm doing it, I don't know.

00:27:01.740 --> 00:27:03.360
- How can I make you believe that-- - Believe it?

00:27:03.360 --> 00:27:04.740
Why shouldn't I believe you, Doctor?

00:27:04.740 --> 00:27:06.400
You're a smart fellow, a college man.

00:27:06.400 --> 00:27:09.430
You probably wouldn't make something out of nothing just to be important.

00:27:09.430 --> 00:27:17.270
Listen, what are we here for? I'll be home.

00:27:17.270 --> 00:27:21.410
You know, my mother always told me if you look deep enough in anybody,

00:27:21.410 --> 00:27:23.670
you'd always find some good, but I don't know.

00:27:23.670 --> 00:27:28.480
With apologies to your mother, that's the second mistake she made.

00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:30.000
I should have seen that one coming.

00:27:30.510 --> 00:27:32.110
- Do you drink coffee, Captain? - Yeah.

00:27:32.110 --> 00:27:33.510
- Come on, I'll buy you a cup. - I'm busy.

00:27:33.510 --> 00:27:35.010
- I want to buy you a cup. - I'm busy.

00:27:35.010 --> 00:27:38.070
Come on, let's see if you can drag that load across the street.

00:27:38.070 --> 00:27:41.630
Let's go.

00:27:41.630 --> 00:27:53.060
- Captain, do you have a family? Are you married? - No.

00:27:53.060 --> 00:27:54.970
My wife died eight years ago.

00:27:54.970 --> 00:27:58.980
- Sorry. - The doctor got said she hadn't aroused her.

00:27:58.980 --> 00:28:00.000
She didn't.

00:28:00.280 --> 00:28:05.620
brain tumor you don't think much of me as a doctor either do you keep asking

00:28:05.620 --> 00:28:12.480
questions doc you finally get answers no mind if i ask why government job civil

00:28:12.480 --> 00:28:18.200
service 30 years of pension what do you make i think it runs about the same as a

00:28:18.200 --> 00:28:26.320
police captain thanks lady see that probably phoned his lawyer sue us for

00:28:26.320 --> 00:28:30.000
false arrest the reason i asked if you have a family was that

00:28:30.380 --> 00:28:33.880
Well, I thought if you had some children, you might realize the seriousness of this.

00:28:33.960 --> 00:28:36.870
- I haven't got any kids. - Well, thousands of people do.

00:28:36.950 --> 00:28:39.030
- And think what could happen to them... - I'll think anything you like,

00:28:39.110 --> 00:28:40.950
but I'll still say I'm doing everything I do.

00:28:41.030 --> 00:28:44.450
Look, this man came off a boat. He was obviously smuggled into the country.

00:28:44.530 --> 00:28:46.170
We've checked every boat, we've combed the waterfront,

00:28:46.250 --> 00:28:48.920
and we're hauling in every man who could possibly know anything about it.

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:51.380
Now, from what I've seen, they may not want to talk to the police.

00:28:51.460 --> 00:28:53.300
Maybe they don't. Maybe they want to talk to their mothers.

00:28:53.380 --> 00:28:55.340
Maybe they want to talk to you. What can I do about it?

00:28:55.420 --> 00:28:57.800
Offer a reward. Promise immunity for information.

00:28:57.880 --> 00:29:00.000
Then get a couple more experts from Washington to help you.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.000
You'll never see the day.

00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:09.390
Do you mind if I do something on my own?

00:29:09.390 --> 00:29:12.430
Yes, I do.

00:29:12.430 --> 00:29:14.800
What am I supposed to do? Just sit here and watch?

00:29:14.800 --> 00:29:16.800
Listen, Captain, I'm taking a chance. You may be right.

00:29:16.800 --> 00:29:18.800
You can take a chance. I know what I'm doing and let me do it.

00:29:18.800 --> 00:29:22.800
As a matter of fact, you'd help us both out if you went home and went to bed.

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:24.800
Okay, I'm not going to argue anymore.

00:29:24.800 --> 00:29:26.910
And I'm not going to wait until the facts pitch out.

00:29:26.910 --> 00:29:30.000
I'm not going to wait until the facts come out.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:33.540
You can't penetrate that thick skull of yours, there just isn't that much time.

00:29:33.540 --> 00:29:35.060
There's for the car.

00:29:35.060 --> 00:29:48.070
You look great.

00:29:48.070 --> 00:29:50.570
You got that stuff all packed, Angie? My suits and them two sweaters?

00:29:50.570 --> 00:29:52.570
I got them. What are they after you for this time?

00:29:52.570 --> 00:29:54.080
Angie, why do you want to talk like that for?

00:29:54.080 --> 00:29:55.580
I told you, it's just the trip. Blackie says we're...

00:29:55.580 --> 00:29:58.580
Blackie, Blackie, he runs you around like a dog on a leash.

00:29:58.580 --> 00:29:59.580
He's my boss, ain't he?

00:29:59.580 --> 00:30:00.000
He's a big boy.

00:30:00.090 --> 00:30:04.010
- He pays me every week-- - He's a bigger boob than you've been saying he was.

00:30:04.010 --> 00:30:05.900
Why don't you stand up to him sometimes?

00:30:05.900 --> 00:30:06.900
Why don't you tell him all?

00:30:06.900 --> 00:30:07.900
Andrew, will you shut up?

00:30:07.900 --> 00:30:08.900
What are you hanging around outside for?

00:30:08.900 --> 00:30:09.900
Why don't you get inside?

00:30:09.900 --> 00:30:11.900
Be alone with that big ape.

00:30:11.900 --> 00:30:13.900
You think I lost my butt?

00:30:13.900 --> 00:30:21.060
Blackie?

00:30:21.060 --> 00:30:24.740
Blackie?

00:30:24.740 --> 00:30:28.430
Hurry up.

00:30:28.430 --> 00:30:28.960
Blackie?

00:30:32.970 --> 00:30:36.170
It wasn't long, was I? I packed everything like you told me.

00:30:36.170 --> 00:30:38.100
Can I bring your stuff down for you, Blackie?

00:30:38.100 --> 00:30:42.480
- Who's that with you? - Just Angie.

00:30:42.480 --> 00:30:56.710
- Is she coming? - She's my wife. What am I going to do?

00:30:56.710 --> 00:30:59.960
First, tell her to get away from them machines.

00:31:00.060 --> 00:31:01.360
Angie, will you get away from there?

00:31:01.640 --> 00:31:03.720
Blackie don't like nobody fooling with them washing machines.

00:31:03.740 --> 00:31:05.560
It's too late. It's all about now.

00:31:05.800 --> 00:31:07.880
Anything I don't like is a smart, crackin' day.

00:31:09.240 --> 00:31:10.140
Hey, get away from there.

00:31:11.950 --> 00:31:12.670
Yes, you.

00:31:13.120 --> 00:31:14.770
What do you want me to do, just stand here?

00:31:15.130 --> 00:31:16.470
You tell her what she's supposed to do.

00:31:16.630 --> 00:31:18.550
Relax, will you, Angie? We'll be leaving in a minute.

00:31:18.790 --> 00:31:19.330
I'll block you.

00:31:19.660 --> 00:31:20.710
You should have stayed single.

00:31:21.050 --> 00:31:22.590
Well, you know how it is. She was workin' at the same...

00:31:22.590 --> 00:31:24.530
It was Pauldy. I told you to bring Pauldy.

00:31:25.390 --> 00:31:26.620
I know you did, Blackie.

00:31:27.480 --> 00:31:30.000
I went right over there. I told him what you said, but he don't want to go.

00:31:31.690 --> 00:31:33.030
- Why don't he want to go, what's the matter with him?

00:31:33.030 --> 00:31:34.230
- I don't know, Blackie.

00:31:34.230 --> 00:31:35.650
He was getting dressed to go out.

00:31:35.650 --> 00:31:37.250
He said he was taking this dame out.

00:31:37.250 --> 00:31:38.330
He said he didn't want to go.

00:31:38.330 --> 00:31:39.650
I told him all about what was happening.

00:31:39.650 --> 00:31:42.260
- Where's he get the dough to go out?

00:31:42.260 --> 00:31:43.200
He never had a quarter.

00:31:43.200 --> 00:31:45.190
You ever know Poldy when he had a quarter?

00:31:45.190 --> 00:31:46.690
- Oh, that's right, he's always borrowing from somebody.

00:31:46.690 --> 00:31:49.420
- So where's he get the dough?

00:31:49.420 --> 00:31:51.240
Why is he all of a sudden taking the dame out?

00:31:51.240 --> 00:31:52.640
You know, I got a hunch about him.

00:31:52.640 --> 00:31:54.490
- You can stay here, Blackie.

00:31:54.490 --> 00:31:56.210
- Yeah, I got a hunch about him.

00:31:56.210 --> 00:31:58.250
- But look, Blackie, let's get going.

00:31:58.250 --> 00:32:00.000
I tell you, they're picking everybody up, everyone.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.470
They ain't gonna pick me up.

00:32:02.470 --> 00:32:04.390
You see their machines? That's business.

00:32:04.390 --> 00:32:07.700
Legitimate even. They ain't gonna pick up a legitimate businessman.

00:32:07.700 --> 00:32:10.400
They're picking up legitimate. They picked me up. They're picking everybody up.

00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:12.160
That's just it. Why?

00:32:12.160 --> 00:32:15.210
Why are they picking everybody up, Fitch? Why?

00:32:15.210 --> 00:32:16.680
I don't know, Blackie, but let's get new.

00:32:16.680 --> 00:32:18.720
You don't know.

00:32:18.720 --> 00:32:23.100
You got a high school education. You're a smart fellow. You don't know. Figure it out.

00:32:23.100 --> 00:32:25.590
This guy Kocek is just a floater.

00:32:25.590 --> 00:32:30.000
He comes in off a boat, gets very unsocial, even pulls a knife that he's gonna use.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:34.700
So they turned the town upside down for one crumb.

00:32:35.830 --> 00:32:40.210
They got every cop in town huffing and puffing, trying to find out who he is.

00:32:40.570 --> 00:32:41.400
Why are they doing that?

00:32:42.120 --> 00:32:43.020
Lucky, I don't know.

00:32:44.720 --> 00:32:46.200
And I'll figure it out for you.

00:32:48.300 --> 00:32:52.140
I got a hunch he brung something in, see?

00:32:52.530 --> 00:32:57.520
I got a hunch he brung something in and they're looking for.

00:33:00.250 --> 00:33:00.970
He ain't got it.

00:33:01.410 --> 00:33:02.120
And you know why?

00:33:04.230 --> 00:33:06.150
Because friend Poldy's got it.

00:33:06.480 --> 00:33:06.840
Poldy?

00:33:06.960 --> 00:33:08.200
Do you think he would do something?

00:33:08.280 --> 00:33:09.340
He was his cousin, wasn't he?

00:33:10.310 --> 00:33:13.070
Told you I had a hunch about that guy and I was right.

00:33:13.270 --> 00:33:14.410
But Poldy's a nice guy.

00:33:14.450 --> 00:33:14.870
He wouldn't do nothing.

00:33:14.870 --> 00:33:16.310
He's trying to put something over on me, Fitch.

00:33:16.940 --> 00:33:20.130
I saved his life and that's how he repays me.

00:33:22.360 --> 00:33:23.940
You know, Fitch, there's one thing I don't like.

00:33:25.400 --> 00:33:26.840
You know what it is?

00:33:27.020 --> 00:33:28.020
Sure, Blackie, sure.

00:33:28.130 --> 00:33:30.000
Somebody trying to put something over on you.

00:33:30.540 --> 00:33:39.400
never liked it. You find Poldy. I want to see him. No, Blacky, no. Let's get out of town.

00:33:39.400 --> 00:33:44.360
I'm scared, I tell you. They'll pick me up again. Stop with that. They picked you up once. They ain't

00:33:44.360 --> 00:33:48.670
going to do it again. Blacky, I don't know where Poldy went. I don't know where to look for him.

00:33:49.040 --> 00:33:54.380
I'm going to get out of town. Look, I just told you I don't like nobody putting anything over on me.

00:33:55.530 --> 00:34:00.000
Killing a youth, Mitch. Poldy ain't leaving town and you ain't leaving me.

00:34:00.480 --> 00:34:01.480
- Okay, Blackie, sure.

00:34:01.480 --> 00:34:02.780
- Get your hands off him, you big ape!

00:34:02.780 --> 00:34:04.380
- Angie, stay away from him!

00:34:05.760 --> 00:34:09.600
- I'll get him, I'll find him.

00:34:09.600 --> 00:34:12.110
- Thank you, Fitch.

00:34:12.110 --> 00:34:13.460
- I swear I will.

00:34:13.460 --> 00:34:15.040
Come on, Angie, let's go.

00:34:15.040 --> 00:34:19.580
- What am I gonna do when them suitcases are packed?

00:34:19.580 --> 00:34:20.460
- Unpack 'em.

00:34:20.460 --> 00:34:21.460
- Come on, Angie, hurry up.

00:34:21.460 --> 00:34:27.170
- Fitch, I hope you're not planning on leaving town anyway.

00:34:27.170 --> 00:34:28.960
I wouldn't do that, where would you go?

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.510
Yeah, that's right. Where would I go?

00:34:32.510 --> 00:34:43.100
Is this the Siemens hiring home?

00:34:43.100 --> 00:34:45.100
Yeah, this is it. They're clowning the ships now.

00:34:45.100 --> 00:34:46.160
Thanks a lot.

00:35:16.000 --> 00:35:21.500
On the Joseph Martin, this General Steamship Company, a Liberty ship, going to Rio, selling at 7 in the morning.

00:35:21.660 --> 00:35:22.720
Two ABs.

00:35:28.380 --> 00:35:30.000
We have 11, 25, and 11.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:34.200
11:27. They're going. They're going. They're gone.

00:35:37.250 --> 00:35:39.550
- Give this guy a favor. - Thank you.

00:35:39.650 --> 00:35:41.650
On the steamship Pelican, Louisiana.

00:35:41.750 --> 00:35:45.250
Steamship Company, a C-2 going to Oklahoma sailing at noon.

00:35:45.370 --> 00:35:48.170
- Two Oilers. - Say, fella, do you mind if I make an announcement?

00:35:48.270 --> 00:35:49.270
Just take a sign.

00:35:49.370 --> 00:35:55.220
11:28 and 11:29. They're going. They're going. They're gone.

00:35:55.680 --> 00:35:57.970
Grab the mic a minute, Leo.

00:36:00.320 --> 00:36:02.400
That's all. Thanks very much.

00:36:02.500 --> 00:36:05.120
Could I have your attention, please?

00:36:05.480 --> 00:36:07.780
Could I have your attention? This is very important.

00:36:08.380 --> 00:36:12.130
I have some pictures of a man here. I'll pass them out right away.

00:36:12.350 --> 00:36:14.130
Would you take care of those, please?

00:36:14.490 --> 00:36:15.780
Would you mind, sir?

00:36:15.880 --> 00:36:17.240
Thank you.

00:36:17.580 --> 00:36:19.600
Now, please take a good look at him.

00:36:20.180 --> 00:36:24.220
I'll pay $50 to anyone who can tell me anything at all about him.

00:36:24.370 --> 00:36:25.420
Anything.

00:36:25.770 --> 00:36:28.560
I'm not from the police, so you can't get into any trouble.

00:36:28.660 --> 00:36:30.000
I just want the information.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.560
and I'm willing to pay for it.

00:36:31.750 --> 00:36:34.400
- Thank you very much. - Thanks an awful lot.

00:36:34.750 --> 00:36:36.720
- Thank you, sir. - Okay, buddy.

00:36:42.840 --> 00:36:46.340
Okay, anybody that's ever seen this man, speak right up, will you?

00:36:46.950 --> 00:36:50.500
- I never saw him before. - I never saw him either.

00:36:50.680 --> 00:36:53.060
Anybody that can tell me anything at all, how about him?

00:36:53.160 --> 00:36:54.960
- I'll see him. - I've never seen him before.

00:36:55.060 --> 00:36:56.400
I've never seen him, Mac.

00:36:57.900 --> 00:36:59.570
You got the dough on you, Johnny?

00:37:00.350 --> 00:37:03.740
- Can you tell me anything? - I can tell you're taking a terrific chance

00:37:03.840 --> 00:37:06.940
flashing that kind of door around this mob. Shipping is tough.

00:37:07.040 --> 00:37:10.440
- You can say that again. - I'm serious about this.

00:37:10.540 --> 00:37:13.730
Any information at all, even if you just think you've ever seen him.

00:37:13.750 --> 00:37:17.420
- What's this fella done, lad? - Nothing. There's no trouble.

00:37:17.490 --> 00:37:21.790
Let me give you a bit of advice. These fellas are not liable to talk around here.

00:37:21.890 --> 00:37:24.660
- What do you mean? - He's ought to be a seaman too.

00:37:24.760 --> 00:37:30.000
- That's right, bud. - I got you. Thanks.

00:37:30.350 --> 00:37:32.220
- No trouble at all.

00:37:32.220 --> 00:37:35.710
- Look, if anybody knows anything about him,

00:37:35.710 --> 00:37:38.050
I'll be at Frank's place right next door here

00:37:38.050 --> 00:37:41.110
until seven o'clock.

00:37:41.110 --> 00:37:43.820
You can ask any questions you want to.

00:37:43.820 --> 00:37:46.740
You can give me the information if you want to do that, okay?

00:37:46.740 --> 00:37:48.140
- You buy the coffee, mate?

00:37:48.140 --> 00:37:50.560
- I'll buy your breakfast, your lunch, and your dinner

00:37:50.560 --> 00:37:53.190
if you can find me anybody who knows this man.

00:37:53.190 --> 00:37:55.690
- We have three limiters coming out of the barnyard.

00:37:55.690 --> 00:37:57.940
We'll meet three full crew.

00:37:57.940 --> 00:38:00.000
On the right hill, volume on the steamship.

00:38:01.690 --> 00:38:04.100
All righty, one boat and the two ordinaries.

00:38:04.100 --> 00:38:06.270
On the boat we have 11:25.

00:38:06.270 --> 00:38:07.770
It's going.

00:38:07.770 --> 00:38:13.840
- Chill that sugar down, will you?

00:38:13.840 --> 00:38:15.340
- Come over those eggs, Frank.

00:38:15.340 --> 00:38:17.840
I gotta make the seven o'clock bus, you hear?

00:38:17.840 --> 00:38:21.670
- I'm coming, I'm coming.

00:38:21.670 --> 00:38:29.160
That's so long.

00:38:47.790 --> 00:38:51.440
- Can I speak to you? - Sure, go right ahead.

00:39:00.570 --> 00:39:02.570
Are you the man who's looking for someone?

00:39:03.040 --> 00:39:05.110
Yeah, as a matter of fact, I was.

00:39:05.890 --> 00:39:11.360
- Someone looking for $50? - That's right.

00:39:13.890 --> 00:39:15.650
He said for you to come with me, will you?

00:39:16.130 --> 00:39:17.430
He said? Who's he?

00:39:18.850 --> 00:39:23.490
- Are you coming? - Yeah.

00:40:02.040 --> 00:40:04.660
- It's cold on here by the wall. - Yeah.

00:40:04.680 --> 00:40:24.160
- What do you want him to know? - I want to know if your friend has ever seen this man.

00:40:24.420 --> 00:40:28.320
- Why? - Because obviously I want to find out about him.

00:40:28.640 --> 00:40:30.000
- Do something wrong? - No.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:32.300
No, he did nothing wrong. Nobody's going to get into any trouble.

00:40:32.400 --> 00:40:34.920
- Have you ever seen him? - No.

00:40:35.020 --> 00:40:36.520
- Come on, come on. - No, I've never seen him.

00:40:36.620 --> 00:40:40.950
- Where is this friend of yours? - He wanted to know why you were looking.

00:40:41.220 --> 00:40:46.180
He did, huh? Well, if he wants to know so badly, let him come and ask me.

00:40:47.520 --> 00:40:50.570
- What are you doing here? - Where'd you come from?

00:40:50.670 --> 00:40:52.750
Cut it out.

00:40:52.850 --> 00:40:54.950
- Who are you, a cop? - I'm with the public health service.

00:40:55.050 --> 00:40:56.560
- I'm a doctor. - A doctor?

00:40:56.660 --> 00:41:00.000
That's right, I'm a doctor. I want to know who this man is, how he got into the country.

00:41:00.030 --> 00:41:01.850
A lot of wanting for 50 bucks.

00:41:01.850 --> 00:41:03.850
That's all you're gonna get. Take it or leave it.

00:41:03.850 --> 00:41:05.850
Charlie, I told you not to drink anymore.

00:41:05.850 --> 00:41:07.850
I told you yesterday to keep away from it.

00:41:07.850 --> 00:41:10.090
Did you bring this man into the country?

00:41:10.090 --> 00:41:11.330
No.

00:41:11.330 --> 00:41:13.330
Because if you did, there's a good chance you're gonna die in about four days.

00:41:13.330 --> 00:41:15.330
Who are you trying to kid?

00:41:15.330 --> 00:41:17.330
Nobody. I'm trying to save you.

00:41:17.330 --> 00:41:19.540
You're a sailor. Did you ever hear a plague?

00:41:19.540 --> 00:41:20.650
Plague?

00:41:20.650 --> 00:41:22.510
This man died of it yesterday morning.

00:41:22.510 --> 00:41:23.510
He's making it up.

00:41:23.510 --> 00:41:24.510
I'm not making it up.

00:41:24.510 --> 00:41:25.510
No, I don't think he...

00:41:25.510 --> 00:41:26.440
He's trying to free me.

00:41:26.440 --> 00:41:28.940
I ain't never seen this guy.

00:41:28.940 --> 00:41:30.000
I ain't been out of Fortentale.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:43.560
Okay. If you didn't bring him in or have any contact with him, then you've got nothing to worry about.

00:41:43.560 --> 00:41:44.380
No, wait.

00:41:44.380 --> 00:41:45.380
Let him go.

00:41:45.380 --> 00:41:46.380
No, I won't.

00:41:46.380 --> 00:41:47.380
Get out of here.

00:41:47.380 --> 00:41:49.380
You told me yourself, Charlie, that the man was sick when you brought him in.

00:41:49.380 --> 00:41:51.380
Why, you stupid little bullock.

00:41:51.380 --> 00:41:54.380
Charlie, please. He's a doctor. He ought to know what he's doing.

00:41:54.380 --> 00:41:58.200
This is $50. This is anti-plague serum.

00:42:06.330 --> 00:42:09.210
Now roll up your sleeve and start talking. Hold this, will ya?

00:42:09.350 --> 00:42:11.620
A guy you want for Tramp out in the Gulf.

00:42:12.600 --> 00:42:14.660
I don't know his name and I know nothing about him.

00:42:16.050 --> 00:42:17.690
I swung the whole deal with one of the mates.

00:42:17.890 --> 00:42:18.890
- What ship? - I don't know.

00:42:19.090 --> 00:42:20.930
- You know? - It was night, I couldn't see.

00:42:21.130 --> 00:42:22.530
- What ship? - Give him the shot, Doc.

00:42:22.730 --> 00:42:24.660
- What's the name of that ship? - I said I don't know.

00:42:24.860 --> 00:42:26.940
Look, sailor, this is the only hypodermy I've gotten.

00:42:27.140 --> 00:42:30.000
It breaks very easily. Now start talking or you're gonna get in the trouble.

00:42:30.280 --> 00:42:31.280
All right.

00:42:31.280 --> 00:42:33.510
It was a Nile queen.

00:42:33.510 --> 00:42:34.510
You sure?

00:42:34.510 --> 00:42:35.510
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:42:35.510 --> 00:42:36.510
All right, hold still.

00:42:36.510 --> 00:42:38.970
Roll up this thing.

00:42:38.970 --> 00:42:53.450
Now, hold still.

00:42:53.450 --> 00:43:00.000
Bring him aboard.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:01.400
I'm going to finish my practice.

00:43:01.660 --> 00:43:02.160
All right, sir.

00:43:04.900 --> 00:43:10.590
Couldn't you have been a forward without your knowledge, Captain?

00:43:10.590 --> 00:43:11.370
No, he couldn't.

00:43:11.450 --> 00:43:13.470
This is a waste of your time and mine.

00:43:13.610 --> 00:43:16.830
The sooner you go over the side, the sooner I can get underway again.

00:43:17.300 --> 00:43:20.300
Pass the way to the engine room and stand by and get underway.

00:43:20.460 --> 00:43:20.700
Nothing.

00:43:20.880 --> 00:43:21.720
Did he tell you he did?

00:43:21.940 --> 00:43:22.440
Let's go.

00:43:22.520 --> 00:43:25.530
You've cost me two hours delay already with this evening, too.

00:43:25.550 --> 00:43:28.650
But, Captain, the man I spoke to was positive the ship was the Nile Queen.

00:43:28.650 --> 00:43:30.000
Well, the last time I'm told...

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.220
I'm telling you, I never saw the man in my life.

00:43:32.830 --> 00:43:35.690
Anyone who says he was smuggling off my ship is a liar.

00:43:35.730 --> 00:43:38.110
A man exposed to pneumonic plague doesn't lie.

00:43:38.170 --> 00:43:39.030
I say he did.

00:43:39.150 --> 00:43:39.750
All right, Captain.

00:43:39.750 --> 00:43:41.330
Is he going to call me a liar, too?

00:43:41.330 --> 00:43:42.510
I'm calling you a fool.

00:43:43.360 --> 00:43:45.000
Okay, I'll get off your ship.

00:43:45.310 --> 00:43:48.280
But if that man was aboard you...

00:43:48.280 --> 00:43:52.080
And most of your crew will be dead before you're halfway to Santiago.

00:43:52.480 --> 00:43:53.780
I'll worry about that.

00:43:54.230 --> 00:43:55.810
Take it easy. Take it easy.

00:43:56.010 --> 00:43:57.370
We're in international waters.

00:43:57.610 --> 00:43:58.930
This man is master of this vessel.

00:43:58.970 --> 00:44:00.000
We have no authority here.

00:44:01.950 --> 00:44:03.040
Come on, let's go.

00:44:50.480 --> 00:44:55.800
The tracing's on those beams, as planned, I can guarantee a hundred fifty to a hundred and seventy raps on this ship.

00:44:55.800 --> 00:44:56.800
What did I tell you?

00:44:56.800 --> 00:44:58.430
You men hear that?

00:44:58.430 --> 00:44:59.530
You men hear that?

00:45:00.060 --> 00:45:07.460
rats and they might be carrying plague hey what's going on down there get those men out of there

00:45:07.460 --> 00:45:13.600
all of them get back to work all right boys let's start moving no we want to hear what he's saying

00:45:13.600 --> 00:45:17.680
yeah we want to hear remember what he's saying get moving don't show me

00:45:22.430 --> 00:45:30.000
oh i got the weapons mr and stand by stop bluffing

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:31.760
Captain, you've got plague on this ship.

00:45:31.760 --> 00:45:33.540
You're inciting my men to mutiny.

00:45:33.540 --> 00:45:35.460
Now get off of here before I take action.

00:45:35.460 --> 00:45:36.840
Your men know it's true.

00:45:36.840 --> 00:45:39.600
Wasn't there another man on board who died just last week?

00:45:39.600 --> 00:45:43.140
I'm the master here, and for the last time, I'm telling you, it's dark.

00:45:48.660 --> 00:45:51.640
One of your cooks is down with fever.

00:45:51.640 --> 00:45:53.080
That's just the first one, Captain.

00:45:53.080 --> 00:45:54.800
Now what are you going to do about it?

00:45:54.800 --> 00:45:56.900
What do you want, Mr. General?

00:45:56.900 --> 00:45:59.350
Right now, I want to inoculate every man on board.

00:45:59.350 --> 00:46:00.000
After that, you'll

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:02.300
and quarantine your ship under my men.

00:46:02.300 --> 00:46:03.880
What about the stowaways?

00:46:03.880 --> 00:46:04.880
I didn't have anything to do with them.

00:46:04.880 --> 00:46:06.880
Wouldn't make much difference if you were dead.

00:46:06.880 --> 00:46:07.880
Get the equipment, Paul.

00:46:07.880 --> 00:46:09.880
All right, let's get started.

00:46:09.880 --> 00:46:14.700
- Sailmaker. - Sailmaker, yes.

00:46:14.700 --> 00:46:16.700
You're sure these two men got on at O'Ran?

00:46:16.700 --> 00:46:18.200
They must have.

00:46:18.200 --> 00:46:19.520
It's the only place they could have.

00:46:19.520 --> 00:46:20.520
What about the other man?

00:46:20.520 --> 00:46:23.020
Did anybody see his body after he died?

00:46:23.020 --> 00:46:24.700
Well, he's the sailmaker.

00:46:24.700 --> 00:46:25.700
He sewed him up.

00:46:25.700 --> 00:46:26.200
He might have.

00:46:26.200 --> 00:46:28.210
No, I just dumped him over to sew.

00:46:28.210 --> 00:46:30.000
- Hmm, great. - Secondary infection?

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:32.000
Sure, it's the only possible way.

00:46:32.000 --> 00:46:34.000
Okay, you can move along.

00:46:34.000 --> 00:46:35.110
Think we have enough on this fella?

00:46:35.110 --> 00:46:36.110
Yes, sir.

00:46:36.110 --> 00:46:37.110
Okay, that'll be all for you.

00:46:37.110 --> 00:46:39.110
You come on and sit down here.

00:46:39.110 --> 00:46:41.090
Did you ever see these two men who were in the chain locker?

00:46:41.090 --> 00:46:44.960
Here, you see them every day.

00:46:44.960 --> 00:46:45.960
You see them every day?

00:46:45.960 --> 00:46:46.960
How come?

00:46:46.960 --> 00:46:49.200
The cabin boy, he bring them food.

00:46:49.200 --> 00:46:51.200
Okay, let him talk for himself now.

00:46:51.200 --> 00:46:52.200
You brought them the food every day?

00:46:52.200 --> 00:46:53.200
Yes, sir.

00:46:53.200 --> 00:46:54.200
Did they ever say anything?

00:46:54.200 --> 00:46:57.200
Uh, sure, food stinks. Goodbye.

00:46:58.160 --> 00:47:00.000
This boy just came home.

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:01.760
It just kills you, doesn't it?

00:47:01.840 --> 00:47:03.730
- Are you the cook? - Yes, sir.

00:47:03.800 --> 00:47:05.880
Did they ever talk about anything else?

00:47:05.960 --> 00:47:10.750
No, sir. Only one time they told me to tell the cook to make shish kebab.

00:47:10.830 --> 00:47:14.190
Shish kebab? Do you want a shish kebab?

00:47:14.270 --> 00:47:15.510
Shut up.

00:47:15.590 --> 00:47:17.630
- Do you like shish kebab? - Yes, I'm sure.

00:47:17.710 --> 00:47:20.430
If I knew what shish kebab was, maybe we'd be on the trail or something.

00:47:20.510 --> 00:47:21.510
It's lamb on a skewer.

00:47:21.590 --> 00:47:23.870
Some of the Greek and Armenian restaurants are on town to serve it.

00:47:24.060 --> 00:47:26.800
To tell you the truth, I'm rather fond of it myself.

00:47:26.880 --> 00:47:30.000
That's it. They call me dirty names. They say,

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.300
- They go on shore, sir. - You know on shore?

00:47:32.300 --> 00:47:35.730
- Uh, they know the place. - What's the name of the place?

00:47:35.730 --> 00:47:37.900
Did they say the name of the place?

00:47:37.900 --> 00:47:40.140
- Come on. -

00:47:40.140 --> 00:47:44.750
- Uh, no. Just a restaurant. - Okay, run along.

00:47:44.750 --> 00:47:47.750
Well, I thought maybe we had something there. It might be a little something like that.

00:47:47.750 --> 00:47:54.320
- Now you're asking me the question? - I suppose we'll have to wind up in a policeman's benefit, but I'll have to.

00:48:19.040 --> 00:48:23.970
- Where's the honor of his plan? - Yanni.

00:48:24.210 --> 00:48:25.660
- Sesitunim. - Kalan.

00:48:32.910 --> 00:48:34.570
- What is it? - You're the proprietor?

00:48:34.670 --> 00:48:36.280
- Yes. - John LaFerris?

00:48:36.490 --> 00:48:38.640
- Yes, sir. - You serve Greek food?

00:48:38.720 --> 00:48:42.650
- Anything you like, gentlemen. - We're from the Public Health Service.

00:48:42.750 --> 00:48:44.890
- I don't clean place. I passed inspection last month.

00:48:44.990 --> 00:48:47.490
- No, we're just trying to identify a man, that's all.

00:48:47.590 --> 00:48:49.730
- You know this man? Has he ever come in your place?

00:48:49.750 --> 00:48:58.350
- What do you want him for? - If you don't mind my asking...

00:48:58.450 --> 00:49:00.000
I'm asking you. Do you recognize him?

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.590
He's not across the street.

00:49:02.590 --> 00:49:04.590
You won't get into any trouble, we just want some information.

00:49:04.590 --> 00:49:05.590
I ain't too worried.

00:49:05.590 --> 00:49:07.590
He had an infection, a contagious disease.

00:49:07.590 --> 00:49:11.590
We want to find out who he was, where he went, the people he saw.

00:49:11.590 --> 00:49:13.410
Sure, sure.

00:49:13.410 --> 00:49:14.410
I don't know.

00:49:14.410 --> 00:49:16.780
So many people come here all the time.

00:49:16.780 --> 00:49:20.670
Maybe my wife, I'll ask her.

00:49:20.670 --> 00:49:22.710
Yeah.

00:49:22.710 --> 00:49:29.180
I got a feeling this is going to be very helpful.

00:49:29.180 --> 00:49:29.380
Oh.

00:49:35.050 --> 00:49:37.050
You know this is hopeless, don't you Doc?

00:49:37.050 --> 00:49:39.050
This is about the 15th joint we've been in.

00:49:39.050 --> 00:49:42.050
It's 11 by actual count. What can you suggest?

00:49:42.050 --> 00:49:44.050
Look, we run the whole story in tonight's paper.

00:49:44.050 --> 00:49:45.050
His picture, everything.

00:49:45.050 --> 00:49:48.050
I'll block every road leaving town, cover the bus stations and...

00:49:48.050 --> 00:49:50.160
No.

00:49:50.160 --> 00:49:53.020
You're getting it. Slowly.

00:49:53.020 --> 00:49:56.840
You sure make them stubborn up where you come from.

00:49:56.840 --> 00:49:57.840
That's right.

00:49:57.840 --> 00:50:00.000
He's the man that fell apart.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:02.570
- What about him? - They asked me if I know him.

00:50:02.650 --> 00:50:07.680
- For pity's sake, go and tell him and stop fussing at me. - It's Board of Health.

00:50:07.740 --> 00:50:09.340
They say he's sick.

00:50:09.420 --> 00:50:12.260
Oh, that Board of Health was here last month.

00:50:12.340 --> 00:50:15.260
We paid for our license, so I don't know how we did it.

00:50:15.340 --> 00:50:18.800
- But they say he's sick, bad sick. - So am I sick.

00:50:18.880 --> 00:50:21.340
- But this is contagious. - Contagious?

00:50:21.420 --> 00:50:23.260
You tell them to go and mind their own business.

00:50:23.340 --> 00:50:25.540
We don't know nothing about it.

00:50:25.620 --> 00:50:27.080
Don't stand there.

00:50:27.160 --> 00:50:30.000
- Don't stand there. - What?

00:50:30.350 --> 00:50:33.850
- But the law, we've got to obey the law. - We've never seen them.

00:50:33.950 --> 00:50:35.860
I don't know. I don't like it.

00:50:35.910 --> 00:50:38.960
Oh, John, I've got a headache that's fit to kill me.

00:50:39.020 --> 00:50:41.530
You don't go out there and tell them that we don't know nothing about this...

00:50:41.630 --> 00:50:44.150
and get them out of this place. I'm going to do it myself.

00:50:44.350 --> 00:50:46.780
Stop all this nonsense. Go on and tell them.

00:50:46.900 --> 00:50:51.700
Okay, Rita, okay. I'll tell them. I'll tell them.

00:50:51.900 --> 00:50:53.400
She doesn't know him either.

00:50:53.740 --> 00:50:55.540
Why don't you leave the picture? He may come sometime.

00:50:55.640 --> 00:50:58.960
I don't think he'll be around for a while.

00:51:11.960 --> 00:51:15.080
They're in there, Blackie, in the back.

00:51:15.090 --> 00:51:18.280
- They found Boldy, huh? - Yes. I tipped him off where to go.

00:51:18.520 --> 00:51:21.970
- Did you take care of that other matter, Pat? - I stayed all night, watched the house.

00:51:22.070 --> 00:51:24.470
- What happened? - She came home early, not a peep out of us.

00:51:24.570 --> 00:51:30.000
- Good. Here you are, Pat. - No, no thanks. No, no, Blackie, no, no.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:32.530
- God bless you, Black. - God bless you.

00:51:32.950 --> 00:51:35.050
Hey! You gotta wait, man!

00:51:35.050 --> 00:51:36.970
This is my beef. Get away!

00:51:36.970 --> 00:51:45.460
Hey, Pacific.

00:51:45.460 --> 00:51:47.150
Black, I found him. See, I found him.

00:51:47.150 --> 00:51:51.830
That told me how you found him. What's that smell in here?

00:51:51.830 --> 00:51:53.800
Have you been trying something on your hair again?

00:51:53.800 --> 00:51:56.990
No, Black, I ain't put nothing on.

00:51:56.990 --> 00:51:59.640
- You touched that yet? - No, Black.

00:52:06.910 --> 00:52:10.120
- Hiya, Blackie. - Hello, Poldy. What's the matter?

00:52:10.320 --> 00:52:14.320
- I'm sick. Don't feel so good. - You felt good enough to stay out last night and run me all over town.

00:52:14.520 --> 00:52:17.790
- Gave him a little bit of trouble, huh, Poldy? - Who's this?

00:52:17.990 --> 00:52:19.520
- My kid brother, Vincent. - Let's lose him.

00:52:19.710 --> 00:52:21.710
I told you I don't feel good. I need somebody with me.

00:52:21.910 --> 00:52:24.710
- We'll wit you, Poldy. Blow out of here, kid. - Who asked you, Curly?

00:52:24.910 --> 00:52:27.590
- Hit the road before I... - Be objectionable, Fitch.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:32.670
- Nice to know you, Vince. - Thanks, Blackie.

00:52:32.770 --> 00:52:35.610
- Do you want to do Blackie a favor, kid? - Yeah, I guess so.

00:52:35.710 --> 00:52:39.830
Run out and get me a scratch, huh? Maybe I got something I can put a couple of bucks on for you.

00:52:40.250 --> 00:52:46.510
Thanks, Blackie. Thanks, Blackie.

00:52:47.570 --> 00:52:51.890
You don't feel good, huh, Poldy? I got a pretty good doctor. Maybe he can take a look at you.

00:52:51.990 --> 00:52:55.730
I'll be all right. I'm just sort of cold in my head. I ought to be in bed.

00:52:55.830 --> 00:52:57.030
- Ah! - Ah, what?

00:52:57.130 --> 00:52:59.340
- Ah, you're always bellyaching, that's why. - Nobody asked you.

00:52:59.440 --> 00:53:00.000
Leave him alone.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:02.540
Maybe he's got a touch of swamp fever or something.

00:53:02.600 --> 00:53:04.980
Look, Poldy, I wouldn't have had him bother you. Only I wanted to ask...

00:53:05.080 --> 00:53:06.980
About Kochak, I never should have brung him that night.

00:53:07.080 --> 00:53:08.980
I'm sorry, Blackie, but you got your dough and everything.

00:53:09.080 --> 00:53:10.420
I wasn't thinking about him, Poldy.

00:53:10.500 --> 00:53:12.960
But now that you bring it up, tell me...

00:53:13.060 --> 00:53:14.460
He was nothing, honest. He was nothing.

00:53:14.560 --> 00:53:16.660
Just enough to have every cop in town looking for him.

00:53:16.760 --> 00:53:19.280
They're grabbing every guy in sight, whether he's got a record or not.

00:53:19.380 --> 00:53:20.380
Yeah.

00:53:20.390 --> 00:53:23.720
And they even picked up the master criminal here.

00:53:24.030 --> 00:53:28.550
Why do you suppose they're doing that, Poldy?

00:53:28.610 --> 00:53:30.000
No.

00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:33.200
Blackie, it's like I told Fitz, he was a cousin of mine,

00:53:33.240 --> 00:53:34.560
but I don't know nothing else about him.

00:53:34.780 --> 00:53:37.540
Some cousin? He might have killed you if I hadn't been there.

00:53:37.640 --> 00:53:38.500
Yeah, fine cousin.

00:53:38.540 --> 00:53:41.800
Thank you, Blackie, but he didn't bring nothing into the country.

00:53:43.370 --> 00:53:44.980
I mean, he was...

00:53:44.980 --> 00:53:46.120
What made you say that, Paulie?

00:53:46.300 --> 00:53:48.060
I don't know, Blackie, I just thought that...

00:53:48.060 --> 00:53:50.390
Maybe the cops, or maybe you thought that...

00:53:50.390 --> 00:53:53.420
I gotta get out and get some water.

00:53:53.840 --> 00:53:55.080
Sit down, Paulie, here's some water.

00:53:56.010 --> 00:53:57.080
What made you say that?

00:53:57.910 --> 00:54:00.000
I don't know, Blackie, I just thought that...

00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:02.140
- You figured that... - Why would I figure that?

00:54:02.260 --> 00:54:04.800
I don't know, but there was nothing at all.

00:54:04.880 --> 00:54:06.220
- Can't you believe me? - Why should he?

00:54:06.300 --> 00:54:09.260
Don't talk like that, Fitch. All Poldy said was he didn't bring nothing in.

00:54:09.340 --> 00:54:11.390
Poldy ought to know the guy was his cousin.

00:54:13.690 --> 00:54:16.570
He was going to stay with you, wasn't he, Poldy? He left his stuff with you?

00:54:16.650 --> 00:54:18.570
I don't know where he was going to stay.

00:54:18.650 --> 00:54:22.610
Sit down, Poldy. I'm talking to you. It ain't polite to get up with him.

00:54:23.450 --> 00:54:30.000
I thought there was something funny about that shirt that loved Lisbon.

00:54:32.200 --> 00:54:35.930
- When was you in Lisbon last? - You lied to Blackie, Poldy.

00:54:35.930 --> 00:54:39.170
He don't like to be lied to. You know what I mean, Poldy? He don't like it.

00:54:39.170 --> 00:54:42.470
- He just had a couple of shirts. You can have them all. - That's what I smelled. What do you got on you?

00:54:42.470 --> 00:54:47.020
- Nothing. I ain't got nothing. - You're lying again. Perfume.

00:54:47.020 --> 00:54:50.030
Dota go out last night. I'm disappointed in you.

00:54:50.030 --> 00:54:52.940
I treated you like a friend. And look at you.

00:54:52.940 --> 00:54:58.430
- I ain't lying. Honest, I ain't... - You see why I'm always right, Fitch, because I never trust nobody.

00:54:58.430 --> 00:54:59.670
You make an exception and...

00:55:01.020 --> 00:55:03.700
Do you remember how it was when we took Pauly and Cher and Cher and...

00:55:03.700 --> 00:55:06.100
Yeah, that's right, Blackie. What's yours is mine.

00:55:06.320 --> 00:55:09.740
Only friend Pauly doesn't believe that. He's like everybody else, just out for himself.

00:55:09.800 --> 00:55:12.060
No, no, no, that isn't true. I wouldn't do nothing.

00:55:12.060 --> 00:55:12.340
What am I going to do with you, Pauly?

00:55:12.640 --> 00:55:16.970
What would you do if you was in my shoes and a friend double-crossed you? How would you?

00:55:19.200 --> 00:55:20.960
Pauly, hi Anna.

00:55:22.100 --> 00:55:23.500
Blackie, can I see you for just a minute?

00:55:24.400 --> 00:55:26.180
Sure, baby. Anything wrong?

00:55:26.560 --> 00:55:27.380
No, nothing.

00:55:27.590 --> 00:55:28.230
No.

00:55:30.540 --> 00:55:33.970
- What's the matter with you? Why don't you tell him you're making... - No, no nothing, I tell you.

00:55:34.700 --> 00:55:38.900
- Blanky, honey, I just gotta have a hundred dollars. - Sure, honey, if you're early.

00:55:40.170 --> 00:55:44.380
I'll be with you in a minute, kid.

00:55:45.130 --> 00:55:53.430
I thought that thing came in the brush.

00:56:00.000 --> 00:56:02.000
You see, Fitch, didn't I tell you he's been holding out on us?

00:56:02.100 --> 00:56:03.500
I didn't mean to let him get away.

00:56:03.600 --> 00:56:06.000
- That's all right, Fitch, don't get sweaty. - That's all right, Fitch, don't get sweaty.

00:56:06.050 --> 00:56:08.900
Where's he gonna go that we can't find him?

00:56:08.960 --> 00:56:13.470
Come on.

00:56:14.120 --> 00:56:26.740
17, R17, go to seven.

00:56:26.840 --> 00:56:29.600
He's tied up right off the end of the dock here this morning.

00:56:30.640 --> 00:56:35.640
Car 12, Captain Warren, Captain Warren, emergency.

00:56:35.770 --> 00:56:40.150
Woman 6, 1, 2, 4, Governor Nichols.

00:56:40.190 --> 00:56:41.880
High fever case.

00:56:41.910 --> 00:56:47.060
Captain Warren, Captain Warren, please acknowledge.

00:56:47.060 --> 00:56:52.620
The woman called him Charlie. Doesn't that mean anything?

00:56:52.720 --> 00:56:55.520
Not to me, mister. No, I got a nephew named Charlie.

00:56:55.620 --> 00:56:59.570
I'm sure he's a nice fella. That's great.

00:57:00.800 --> 00:57:03.960
Oh, I don't know. That was my last idea.

00:57:04.390 --> 00:57:06.350
- That woman! - What?

00:57:06.470 --> 00:57:08.880
- There's a car! - What is it?

00:57:08.940 --> 00:57:13.350
It's a woman, sick, fever cage, and an emergency car!

00:57:32.560 --> 00:57:39.380
The boys in the patrol car are picking up the husband, Captain.

00:57:39.380 --> 00:57:41.050
I'll have him here in a few minutes.

00:57:41.050 --> 00:57:44.550
Doctor, call to Suey.

00:57:44.550 --> 00:57:47.430
I'll have to quarantine the hole apart, but Gaffney is inoculated.

00:57:47.430 --> 00:57:49.730
Call in and tell him on the hand I want a detail here right away.

00:57:49.730 --> 00:57:52.330
Cover the entrance yourself, nobody in or out but the husband.

00:57:52.330 --> 00:57:53.810
Yes, sir.

00:57:53.810 --> 00:57:55.550
No chance of a mistake.

00:57:55.550 --> 00:57:57.360
Nah, you couldn't miss it.

00:57:57.360 --> 00:58:00.000
Well, Paul, I want all that bedding burned after you get her out.

00:58:00.160 --> 00:58:00.860
Yes, sir.

00:58:01.780 --> 00:58:03.620
What about the death certificate? It's got to be filed.

00:58:03.720 --> 00:58:06.880
The doctor put down a tentative diagnosis of pneumonia with complications.

00:58:07.060 --> 00:58:07.760
That'll do for now.

00:58:07.860 --> 00:58:08.800
How about the body?

00:58:08.940 --> 00:58:10.240
I'll have the board help to take care of it.

00:58:10.320 --> 00:58:12.180
Happy, what do you do here?

00:58:12.780 --> 00:58:14.800
Well, clear these people out of here, I told you.

00:58:14.960 --> 00:58:15.720
That's my wife.

00:58:16.970 --> 00:58:17.560
Rita?

00:58:20.800 --> 00:58:25.530
Where is she?

00:58:26.020 --> 00:58:28.070
What do you do?

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:32.000
- Let me see my wife. - I can't let you go in.

00:58:32.000 --> 00:58:34.380
- What do you do to her? - Your wife is dead.

00:58:34.380 --> 00:58:45.560
- Dead? Dead? You lie. - She's dead, mister.

00:58:45.560 --> 00:58:51.480
This afternoon, the doctor, she said she just don't feel good.

00:58:51.480 --> 00:58:54.040
- I'm sorry. - She...

00:59:04.570 --> 00:59:07.400
- Remember me, Mafferis?

00:59:07.400 --> 00:59:10.170
We showed you a picture of a man and asked if you knew him.

00:59:10.170 --> 00:59:11.370
You lied to us. Who was he?

00:59:11.370 --> 00:59:13.210
- I don't know. I don't know. - If you told us the truth,

00:59:13.210 --> 00:59:14.710
there's a chance your wife might not have died.

00:59:14.710 --> 00:59:17.050
- I don't know! - I don't know.

00:59:17.050 --> 00:59:19.520
Look, Mafferis, I want to know about this man.

00:59:19.520 --> 00:59:21.360
He had the disease that killed your wife.

00:59:21.360 --> 00:59:22.570
Now, who was he?

00:59:22.570 --> 00:59:24.570
- His disease killed my wife? - Yes.

00:59:24.570 --> 00:59:26.720
Now, who was he? Who was he? Who was he?

00:59:26.720 --> 00:59:28.640
Kocak. His name was Kocak.

00:59:28.640 --> 00:59:30.000
I don't know him. Paul brought him home.

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:32.400
- He was told me. - He was told me.

00:59:32.500 --> 00:59:34.530
- Where does he live? - Where does he live?

00:59:34.610 --> 00:59:36.280
- Gloria Hotel. - I guess.

00:59:36.370 --> 00:59:43.470
Come on, there's nothing you can do for him. Let's go.

00:59:43.480 --> 00:59:51.650
I've worked with Gatney. This place is quarantined.

00:59:51.750 --> 00:59:54.400
Get the address of Maffarel's restaurant. Quarantine man.

00:59:54.500 --> 00:59:57.410
Then try and get a list of everybody who's been in there in the past three days.

00:59:57.510 --> 00:59:59.210
- Yes, sir. - I don't know how many people have been here.

00:59:59.310 --> 01:00:00.000
It's getting pretty rough.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:02.000
Oh, look, you stay here and take charge, will ya, Ben?

01:00:02.000 --> 01:00:03.000
Send for any help you need.

01:00:03.000 --> 01:00:04.000
Right.

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:04.950
Nobody in or out.

01:00:04.950 --> 01:00:05.950
Nobody.

01:00:05.950 --> 01:00:06.840
Come on.

01:00:06.840 --> 01:00:09.170
Gloria Hotel, Ben.

01:00:09.170 --> 01:00:16.410
Gloria Hotel, huh?

01:00:16.410 --> 01:00:17.860
Thanks.

01:00:31.790 --> 01:00:32.750
Nobody in or out.

01:00:32.830 --> 01:00:33.150
Nobody.

01:00:33.290 --> 01:00:33.730
Come on.

01:00:34.550 --> 01:00:42.970
I'm looking for a fellow named Poldy.

01:00:43.050 --> 01:00:43.910
He's not up in his room.

01:00:43.990 --> 01:00:44.710
Where's his room?

01:00:44.930 --> 01:00:45.790
All right, follow me.

01:00:48.240 --> 01:00:55.040
Never mind why I want him, I want him.

01:00:55.120 --> 01:00:56.040
I swear to you, Captain.

01:00:56.280 --> 01:00:58.550
If I know the guy has a record, I never take him in.

01:00:58.730 --> 01:01:00.000
I run a clean establishment.

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:03.000
Yeah, I know. Nothing but retired millionaires and honeymoors.

01:01:03.000 --> 01:01:05.500
Oh, no, Cap. You know I wouldn't have nobody in here...

01:01:05.500 --> 01:01:08.000
Well, we pulled three hoodlums out of here last month.

01:01:08.000 --> 01:01:09.500
Now, who knew this man?

01:01:09.500 --> 01:01:12.130
Nobody, Cap. Honest. Nobody.

01:01:12.130 --> 01:01:15.280
The guy just comes in for a room, and I...

01:01:15.280 --> 01:01:19.780
Just a minute. Just a minute. I just do remember.

01:01:19.780 --> 01:01:21.280
He just does remember.

01:01:21.280 --> 01:01:22.780
A couple of guys were looking for him today.

01:01:22.780 --> 01:01:23.780
Who were they?

01:01:23.780 --> 01:01:28.040
No, I... I don't know. Honest. I don't know.

01:01:28.040 --> 01:01:29.920
You've got to believe me.

01:01:30.220 --> 01:01:33.020
Why? Come on, let's get out of here.

01:01:33.140 --> 01:01:35.620
You better get both of us in trouble, so why don't you be a nice fellow?

01:01:35.740 --> 01:01:38.020
Why don't you take your big hands off me and knock off?

01:01:38.140 --> 01:01:39.140
I'm on you, Neff, you hear me?

01:01:39.260 --> 01:01:41.580
I hear you, that's the trouble. I can't seem to tune you out.

01:01:41.700 --> 01:01:43.120
All right, that's enough.

01:01:43.190 --> 01:01:46.260
Oh, Neff, I didn't know you lived here too.

01:01:46.590 --> 01:01:49.030
I'm ready for your statement on this story now, Doctor.

01:01:49.150 --> 01:01:51.060
- What story is that, Neff? - Oh, cut it out.

01:01:51.090 --> 01:01:52.950
You think I've been walking around with my head in a bag,

01:01:53.070 --> 01:01:55.710
you and the public health service turning this town upside down,

01:01:55.830 --> 01:01:58.740
a murdered hoodlum, a ship in quarantine, and now a woman dead?

01:01:58.800 --> 01:02:00.000
An idiot could figure it out.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:01.800
You qualify, what do you figure?

01:02:01.970 --> 01:02:05.010
I figured the guy had smallpox or cholera or something like that.

01:02:05.120 --> 01:02:08.460
And I want to know why this story wasn't released to the press.

01:02:08.660 --> 01:02:10.060
- Listen, Neff. - Wait a minute, Warren.

01:02:10.540 --> 01:02:18.810
Now look, Neff, it isn't smallpox and it isn't cholera.

01:02:20.310 --> 01:02:22.390
It's plague. You mind, plague.

01:02:23.300 --> 01:02:27.140
Plague?

01:02:27.270 --> 01:02:29.290
That's why we can't let you have the story.

01:02:31.470 --> 01:02:34.410
- You can't let me have it. - That's right.

01:02:34.660 --> 01:02:41.000
- With a chance of an epidemic? - I knew you guys were crazy, but...

01:02:41.100 --> 01:02:43.700
- Wait a minute, Neff, wait a minute. - Wait for what?

01:02:43.800 --> 01:02:48.760
Somebody else to die? Not much. You've already wasted a day and a half.

01:02:48.860 --> 01:02:52.060
- I'm sorry, but I can't let you print this story. - You can't let me print it.

01:02:52.160 --> 01:02:54.070
- Since when have you been making the rules? - I represent the public health service.

01:02:54.170 --> 01:02:57.170
Well, I represent the public, and they've got a right to know what's going on.

01:02:57.270 --> 01:03:00.000
- And no two-bit civil servant is going to stop me. - Regardless of your opinion,

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:01.500
I've got to do what I think is best.

01:03:01.600 --> 01:03:04.000
Did you do what you thought was best for that woman who just died?

01:03:04.100 --> 01:03:08.160
If the doctor had known what was going on, couldn't he have saved her? Couldn't he?

01:03:08.560 --> 01:03:10.540
- I don't know. - You don't know.

01:03:10.620 --> 01:03:12.820
And because you don't know, you don't want anybody else to know.

01:03:12.920 --> 01:03:15.160
- Well, there's a chance we could get... - You bet there is.

01:03:15.330 --> 01:03:18.430
And don't think for a minute that everybody in this town isn't going to get it.

01:03:18.530 --> 01:03:21.930
Oh, drop it. If your editor's got the story, let him go ahead and print it.

01:03:22.030 --> 01:03:24.430
Well, my editor doesn't have it, but he's going to get it.

01:03:24.530 --> 01:03:27.190
Oh, he doesn't have it, eh? What do you know?

01:03:31.020 --> 01:03:32.220
- Take him. - A pleasure.

01:03:32.300 --> 01:03:34.880
- Oh, wait a minute. Warren, what do you think you're trying to fall? - He speaks to no one.

01:03:34.960 --> 01:03:37.800
- What's the charge, Warren? - Loitering, public nuisance, anything you like.

01:03:37.880 --> 01:03:41.590
- You're crazy. I'll have your badge for this, Warren. - It's getting stuffy if this joint take him out.

01:03:41.620 --> 01:03:47.650
- You'll be walking a beast, you're lucky. - No!

01:03:51.690 --> 01:03:54.570
If I'd been busted by every newspaper man to try to get my bars,

01:03:54.650 --> 01:03:58.290
I'd be mopping floors in the hall of justice years ago. Come on.

01:04:03.290 --> 01:04:05.890
Can that reporter really make trouble for it?

01:04:06.010 --> 01:04:07.830
Trouble? Where you been living, mister?

01:04:07.930 --> 01:04:10.130
That newspaper wanted to put the pressure on him.

01:04:10.230 --> 01:04:12.130
He'd be lucky if he could get a job mopping floors.

01:04:12.230 --> 01:04:13.280
Let's go, Bill.

01:04:34.030 --> 01:04:38.500
- Clint, before I heard of you... - Don't come any closer, honey.

01:04:38.600 --> 01:04:39.570
You better stay right up there.

01:04:39.700 --> 01:04:42.840
- Another contagion case, huh? - Yep.

01:04:42.900 --> 01:04:46.630
Another uniform to be decontaminated.

01:04:46.710 --> 01:04:48.280
Some fun, huh?

01:04:48.800 --> 01:04:50.820
You didn't catch it yourself, did you?

01:04:50.920 --> 01:04:52.370
You look a little beat.

01:04:52.410 --> 01:04:54.740
Yeah, I look so good normally.

01:05:00.220 --> 01:05:03.040
- I didn't pay it. - You can pay it tomorrow.

01:05:03.240 --> 01:05:06.040
No, I can't pay it tomorrow, and I can't pay it the next day.

01:05:06.140 --> 01:05:08.970
I spent the money. Now, will you please just forget about that bill?

01:05:09.380 --> 01:05:12.770
When I get the dough, I'll pay it. Just stop pestering me about it.

01:05:13.000 --> 01:05:17.830
- Finn, honey, I didn't say anything. - Yeah, I know.

01:05:17.860 --> 01:05:21.730
Whenever you're tired, you always seem to think I'm scolding.

01:05:21.830 --> 01:05:24.640
- Yeah, I know. I'm sorry. - And I wasn't.

01:05:24.740 --> 01:05:27.590
- I know. You're right. - What happened?

01:05:27.880 --> 01:05:30.000
I gave it to somebody.

01:05:30.600 --> 01:05:34.240
And I wasn't... I wasn't talking about the money.

01:05:35.880 --> 01:05:39.480
Well, anyway, I spent it on something for the department.

01:05:39.880 --> 01:05:42.910
You can put in a voucher or whatever they call it.

01:05:43.650 --> 01:05:48.150
As far as I know, nobody's yet figured out a way to get money back from the U.S. government.

01:05:48.780 --> 01:05:51.650
- Quickly that is. - I'll make up the cop for you.

01:05:51.750 --> 01:05:54.220
- No, I've got to go right out again. - Go right out.

01:05:54.320 --> 01:05:57.100
Look, be a good kid and make me some coffee, will you?

01:05:57.200 --> 01:06:00.000
- How about some nice hot soup? - Just coffee.

01:06:00.380 --> 01:06:01.440
- Clutching? - Coffee.

01:06:50.250 --> 01:06:51.970
Nancy, I told you I can't sleep.

01:06:52.050 --> 01:06:53.850
I have to take a shower and get out of here.

01:06:54.150 --> 01:06:57.050
- Did you sleep last night? - Last night?

01:06:58.080 --> 01:07:00.000
Yeah, sure, I guess I must have.

01:07:01.820 --> 01:07:04.090
- I didn't call you, did I? - That's all right.

01:07:04.090 --> 01:07:10.320
I didn't think. It's a plague case, pneumonic.

01:07:10.320 --> 01:07:12.210
Plague? Here in New Orleans?

01:07:12.210 --> 01:07:14.600
Yeah, a woman died of it tonight.

01:07:14.600 --> 01:07:16.930
Whoever's carrying it's still wandering around.

01:07:16.930 --> 01:07:21.280
Well, at least they have you. You've been through it.

01:07:21.280 --> 01:07:23.940
You know how to handle it.

01:07:23.940 --> 01:07:27.180
Now look, hon, let's not belittle Miss Sunshine.

01:07:27.180 --> 01:07:29.730
All right, all right.

01:07:32.140 --> 01:07:35.270
Why don't you lie down just for an hour or two?

01:07:35.350 --> 01:07:39.010
Gaffney's waiting for me at the office. He doesn't let me sleep either.

01:07:39.090 --> 01:07:40.930
Gaffney can wait. He's younger than you are.

01:07:41.010 --> 01:07:43.810
Maybe Methuselah's younger than I am tonight.

01:07:43.890 --> 01:07:46.740
- What's eating you, anyway? - Nothing.

01:07:46.820 --> 01:07:49.340
- Come on. - I'm all right.

01:07:49.420 --> 01:07:53.020
There's a lot of gas. I'm tired. I'm fed up.

01:07:53.100 --> 01:07:56.350
Well, if you won't lie down, at least sit.

01:07:56.430 --> 01:07:58.850
- You're making me tired standing there. - Stick around.

01:07:58.930 --> 01:08:00.000
I've got to get the coffee.

01:08:00.800 --> 01:08:03.800
I'm just afraid if I sit down the next thing I'll lie down.

01:08:03.900 --> 01:08:08.500
If I lie down, sure is there worms and little green apples, I'll fall asleep.

01:08:08.550 --> 01:08:12.370
If I fall asleep, I'm dead.

01:08:12.390 --> 01:08:17.760
- Now you're cooking. - Just don't let me fall asleep.

01:08:17.850 --> 01:08:19.680
I'll watch you.

01:08:20.900 --> 01:08:25.220
You know, the day I took a perfectly nice guy, a cop.

01:08:25.580 --> 01:08:28.580
Not the smartest guy in the world, but who is?

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:33.160
I push him around, make a lot of smart cracks about him.

01:08:33.240 --> 01:08:36.130
I tell him off all day long.

01:08:36.210 --> 01:08:39.700
He winds up proving he's four times the man I'll ever be.

01:08:40.240 --> 01:08:42.760
- I don't believe. - Why do I do that?

01:08:45.150 --> 01:08:47.780
- You're tired now. - All right, so I'm tired.

01:08:47.860 --> 01:08:50.670
But you know what I mean.

01:08:52.020 --> 01:08:53.650
Yeah, I guess I do.

01:08:56.270 --> 01:08:58.580
Yeah, I do the same thing to you, don't I?

01:08:59.440 --> 01:09:00.000
Yes.

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:00.400
You do.

01:09:00.870 --> 01:09:01.270
Well?

01:09:03.080 --> 01:09:08.390
Well, Clint, you're not a kid anymore, and you ought to stop thinking like one.

01:09:08.690 --> 01:09:09.320
What do you mean?

01:09:11.070 --> 01:09:13.490
Well, like those jobs you're always talking about.

01:09:14.120 --> 01:09:19.800
Arabian pipelines, or expeditions to Chile as medical advisor, or, you know.

01:09:20.530 --> 01:09:23.980
Yeah, what you want to say is that I'm a bust, and I ought to forget about them.

01:09:24.020 --> 01:09:24.980
That's what you mean, isn't it?

01:09:25.060 --> 01:09:26.720
That's exactly what I don't mean.

01:09:28.020 --> 01:09:30.000
You might get an offer like that tomorrow, and you'd be perfect.

01:09:30.030 --> 01:09:32.210
But that's a chance and it's in the future.

01:09:32.210 --> 01:09:34.210
You can't spend the rest of your life...

01:09:34.210 --> 01:09:38.660
You know, you're a pretty lucky guy right this minute.

01:09:38.660 --> 01:09:42.530
Lucky? Please smoke.

01:09:42.530 --> 01:09:43.450
You are.

01:09:43.450 --> 01:09:45.410
You've done exactly what you planned you were going to do

01:09:45.410 --> 01:09:47.410
when you were a junior in medical school.

01:09:47.410 --> 01:09:49.430
How many people can say that?

01:09:49.430 --> 01:09:50.470
I don't know.

01:09:50.470 --> 01:09:53.470
But I do know I've got exactly $38 in the savings account.

01:09:53.470 --> 01:09:57.010
So, every once in a while you...

01:09:57.010 --> 01:10:00.000
you get a guilty feeling that...

01:10:00.760 --> 01:10:10.110
That you've been missing out or that you owe something to me or to Tommy or somebody or other.

01:10:11.000 --> 01:10:13.380
Then you take it out on whoever happens to be around.

01:10:16.670 --> 01:10:17.870
Mostly I'm around.

01:10:21.570 --> 01:10:24.190
So?

01:10:26.320 --> 01:10:30.000
So stop feeling sorry for yourself.

01:10:31.530 --> 01:10:33.700
- Yes, ma'am. - And don't get smart with me.

01:10:33.700 --> 01:10:36.750
If there's a plague here, you're the most important guy in town.

01:10:36.750 --> 01:10:43.210
- And not only to me. - Yes, ma'am. So?

01:10:43.210 --> 01:10:46.550
So that's all.

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:04.960
- You'd be surprised. - That's what needs a lot of time for thinking.

01:11:05.160 --> 01:11:12.750
Some of it I thought up a few weeks ago,

01:11:12.950 --> 01:11:19.520
about the time I decided that Tommy wasn't going to be an only child anymore.

01:11:19.720 --> 01:11:28.900
- You decided what? - You heard me.

01:11:31.310 --> 01:11:41.040
- For Pete's sake. - Do you mind?

01:11:41.140 --> 01:11:45.380
Son of a gun.

01:11:45.480 --> 01:11:51.740
You said yourself that it was bad for Tommy to be an only child.

01:11:52.040 --> 01:11:54.830
- Oh, what do you know? - And aside from Tommy...

01:11:54.930 --> 01:11:58.130
You're going to stay away from me, honey.

01:12:00.090 --> 01:12:09.570
from Tommy I have no intention of being too old to enjoy my grandchildren about

01:12:09.570 --> 01:12:22.570
the money plan to work it out it's the reason I did it was because I knew you

01:12:22.570 --> 01:12:30.000
really wanted I like you can't it's only fair that

01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:34.440
that you get some of the things you want.

01:12:34.440 --> 01:12:36.020
Yes, that's the real reason.

01:13:04.220 --> 01:13:09.410
- Hey! What's up? - I don't know, but it ain't good.

01:13:09.490 --> 01:13:11.090
- What's going on? - I said I don't know.

01:13:11.170 --> 01:13:13.410
They just told me to get you and bring you over here.

01:13:14.670 --> 01:13:20.750
Sorry I had to call you here, but my office and my home are crawling with reporters.

01:13:20.890 --> 01:13:22.670
Now I find you've arrested one.

01:13:22.870 --> 01:13:25.290
What's the matter with you, Warren? Have you lost your mind?

01:13:25.820 --> 01:13:29.190
- If the desk sergeant hadn't made a mistake, he'd be there still. - Yeah, I know.

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:32.460
- What imbecility... - He did it on my authority, Mr. Mayor.

01:13:32.580 --> 01:13:33.680
- Your authority? - Yes, sir.

01:13:33.760 --> 01:13:35.300
What authority is that?

01:13:36.360 --> 01:13:38.490
You're an advisor here, doctor, a guest.

01:13:38.640 --> 01:13:42.100
And you can oblige me by confining your authority to your own duties.

01:13:42.610 --> 01:13:45.000
Where's Mackie? We can't fool around with this any longer.

01:13:45.100 --> 01:13:46.870
I told him to get over here right away.

01:13:46.950 --> 01:13:48.350
He should be here any minute now.

01:13:48.450 --> 01:13:50.150
All I want is a simple statement of fact.

01:13:50.250 --> 01:13:51.650
That shouldn't take him too long.

01:13:51.750 --> 01:13:54.450
Mr. Mayor, we already got a line on one of the dead man's friends.

01:13:54.550 --> 01:13:56.560
- His name is Poli. - Have you made any arrest yet?

01:13:56.730 --> 01:13:57.940
- No, sir. - When will you?

01:13:58.040 --> 01:14:00.000
- Well, it's hard to go out... - I'm sorry, we can't wait that long.

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:02.080
Sorry about the delay.

01:14:02.080 --> 01:14:03.200
Yeah.

01:14:03.200 --> 01:14:04.200
Have you got it with you?

01:14:04.200 --> 01:14:05.200
Yes, sir. Best I could do.

01:14:05.200 --> 01:14:06.200
How are you, Doctor?

01:14:06.200 --> 01:14:07.200
About the same.

01:14:07.200 --> 01:14:08.200
That's all I want.

01:14:08.200 --> 01:14:11.140
I had Mackie make up a statement,

01:14:11.140 --> 01:14:13.140
a complete explanation of the facts as they stand.

01:14:13.140 --> 01:14:15.350
Before I give it to Neff here,

01:14:15.350 --> 01:14:18.210
I want a confirmation from you that the disease can be contained

01:14:18.210 --> 01:14:20.210
and there's no reason for panic.

01:14:20.210 --> 01:14:22.210
Our only chance for full cooperation, Clint,

01:14:22.210 --> 01:14:24.210
is to inform the public.

01:14:24.210 --> 01:14:26.350
You agree?

01:14:26.350 --> 01:14:27.530
No.

01:14:27.530 --> 01:14:30.000
The minute he prints it, the men we're looking for will leave the city.

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:31.760
I've told you once and I'll tell you again.

01:14:32.250 --> 01:14:36.650
Anyone leaving here with plague endangers the entire country.

01:14:36.770 --> 01:14:38.510
The entire country hasn't got it we have.

01:14:38.530 --> 01:14:39.810
A woman died here last night.

01:14:40.390 --> 01:14:42.170
This problem lies right here in our own community.

01:14:42.700 --> 01:14:44.000
Community? What community?

01:14:44.120 --> 01:14:45.680
Do you think you're living in the Middle Ages?

01:14:45.860 --> 01:14:46.400
Oh, come now.

01:14:46.400 --> 01:14:49.820
Anybody that leaves here can be in any city in the country within ten hours.

01:14:50.060 --> 01:14:52.300
I could leave here today and I could be in Africa tomorrow.

01:14:52.640 --> 01:14:54.780
And whatever disease I had would go right with me.

01:14:54.800 --> 01:14:55.460
I know that.

01:14:55.540 --> 01:14:57.580
Then think of it when you're talking about communities.

01:14:57.580 --> 01:14:59.640
We're all in a community, the same one.

01:15:05.790 --> 01:15:08.770
- Give me a seat. - Take a bag.

01:15:10.040 --> 01:15:11.560
- Can I go now? - All right.

01:15:21.880 --> 01:15:24.940
About four more hours before the morning edition.

01:15:25.810 --> 01:15:29.670
- Then I'm wasting my time here. - Do what you can, Tom.

01:15:30.380 --> 01:15:32.310
I couldn't hold Neff.

01:15:32.310 --> 01:15:35.560
Strangely enough, I find myself in complete agreement with you.

01:15:35.560 --> 01:15:37.130
But I couldn't hold him.

01:15:37.130 --> 01:15:39.230
He can color a story any way he wants.

01:15:39.230 --> 01:15:41.330
Yes, he can, but that's his privilege.

01:15:41.330 --> 01:15:43.150
I won't take it away from him.

01:15:43.150 --> 01:15:46.050
I won't say it isn't better that way.

01:15:46.050 --> 01:15:46.850
What is it, Bob?

01:15:46.850 --> 01:15:48.440
Mind if I take off now, sir?

01:15:48.440 --> 01:15:50.940
All right, but I want to be on the radio in the morning at 9 o'clock.

01:15:50.940 --> 01:15:52.670
I'll be here by then, sir.

01:15:52.670 --> 01:15:54.510
I'm not going to lie to you,

01:15:54.510 --> 01:15:56.340
taking the kids upriver to their grandmothers.

01:16:01.240 --> 01:16:03.580
I'll be in your office by 8:30, but I've got to do it.

01:16:03.580 --> 01:16:09.260
- All right. - Well, here we go.

01:16:09.260 --> 01:16:11.360
Don't get any wrong ideas.

01:16:11.360 --> 01:16:13.480
He'll be there in the morning, and you'll stay there.

01:16:13.480 --> 01:16:18.060
Yeah, sure he will. And kids are kids.

01:16:18.060 --> 01:16:21.290
Nevertheless, here we go.

01:16:21.290 --> 01:16:24.380
- Want some coffee? - No, I don't think so.

01:16:24.380 --> 01:16:27.250
Tell you the truth, I'm scared to death.

01:16:27.250 --> 01:16:29.830
I want to call Washington and start getting some help in here.

01:16:37.870 --> 01:16:43.050
Well, Dan, I seem to remember you as the guy who talked me into running for this office.

01:16:43.600 --> 01:16:46.550
I was hoping you'd forget that.

01:16:52.740 --> 01:16:58.740
Mama, send Vince. I'll be right over her.

01:17:07.610 --> 01:17:12.570
This is Poldy's mother, this is Blackie, his best friend, he wants to help him.

01:17:12.570 --> 01:17:15.530
Yes, I heard he was sick, but I can't find him, Mama.

01:17:15.530 --> 01:17:17.530
He's not in his room, I was worried about him.

01:17:17.530 --> 01:17:22.090
No, no, he's home, always, when he's sick, he comes home.

01:17:22.090 --> 01:17:24.090
But he's dying this time.

01:17:24.090 --> 01:17:27.040
Oh, no, no, Mama, he's not gonna die, I'm not gonna let him.

01:17:27.040 --> 01:17:30.000
I'm gonna send for a doctor for him.

01:17:30.060 --> 01:17:32.720
The neighbors already have sent for somebody.

01:17:32.720 --> 01:17:34.860
Yes, but Mama, this is my doctor. He's the best.

01:17:34.860 --> 01:17:36.360
He'll make Poldy well, you'll see.

01:17:36.360 --> 01:17:38.790
Now you tell Vince to go and get him, huh?

01:17:38.790 --> 01:17:40.630
You see if Vince gets the doctor.

01:17:40.630 --> 01:17:43.120
- Say, where did Fitch say he was going? - He went to breakfast.

01:17:43.120 --> 01:17:45.330
He didn't go to breakfast. I've been looking for him.

01:17:45.330 --> 01:17:47.030
I'll find him and bring him over. You hurry up.

01:17:47.030 --> 01:17:49.660
God bless you, Blackie. God bless you.

01:17:49.660 --> 01:17:53.680
That's all right, Poldy. Drink it up and it'll do you good.

01:17:53.680 --> 01:17:55.230
I'm gonna take care of you.

01:17:55.230 --> 01:17:56.750
It's just you and me, huh, Poldy?

01:17:56.750 --> 01:17:58.800
Just you and me, we're gonna...

01:18:04.380 --> 01:18:06.900
Hiya, Blackie. I was just going to get you.

01:18:06.980 --> 01:18:09.320
I was going to get you, only Paulie was so sick, I didn't want to leave you.

01:18:09.400 --> 01:18:11.940
Shouldn't have done it. Shouldn't have done it.

01:18:12.680 --> 01:18:14.790
He says we shouldn't have done it.

01:18:14.800 --> 01:18:18.950
He says, "What do we do, Blackie?"

01:18:20.860 --> 01:18:23.270
Shouldn't have done it.

01:18:23.370 --> 01:18:24.870
Shouldn't have done it.

01:18:24.950 --> 01:18:26.910
Shouldn't have done it!

01:18:30.090 --> 01:18:32.850
I'm sorry, Pauly, but there's nothing we can do about that anymore.

